ass="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-14&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-14" id="mwLQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLw">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt80" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-15&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-15" id="mwMQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMw">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt85" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-16&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-16" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt90" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-17&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-17" id="mwOQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPA">]</span></span></a></sup></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Project_Verona" title="Project Verona">Project Verona</a><sup about="#mwt93" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Project_Verona_18-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Project Verona&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Project_Verona-18" id="mwPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQA">]</span></span></a></sup></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SPARK_(programming_language)" title="SPARK (programming language)">SPARK</a><sup about="#mwt95" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Jaloyan_19-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Jaloyan&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Jaloyan-19" id="mwQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRA">]</span></span></a></sup></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swift_(programming_language)" title="Swift (programming language)">Swift</a><sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Lattner_20-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Lattner&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Lattner-20" id="mwRQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwRg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRw">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSA">]</span></span></a></sup></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V_(programming_language)" title="V (programming language)">V</a><sup about="#mwt101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-21" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-21&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-21" id="mwSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">]</span></span></a></sup></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zig_(programming_language)" title="Zig (programming language)">Zig</a><sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-22" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-22&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-22" id="mwTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUA">]</span></span></a></sup></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gleam_(programming_language)" title="Gleam (programming language)">Gleam</a><sup about="#mwt109" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Gleam_23-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Gleam&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Gleam-23" id="mwUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUw">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVA">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwVQ"><b id="mwVg">Rust</b> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General-purpose_programming_language" title="General-purpose programming language" id="mwVw">general-purpose</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programming_language" title="Programming language" id="mwWA">programming language</a> which emphasizes <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_performance" title="Computer performance" id="mwWQ">performance</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_safety" title="Type safety" id="mwWg">type safety</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concurrency_(computer_science)" title="Concurrency (computer science)" id="mwWw">concurrency</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_safety" title="Memory safety" id="mwXA">memory safety</a>.</p>

<p id="mwXQ">Rust supports multiple <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programming_paradigm" title="Programming paradigm" id="mwXg">programming paradigms</a>. It was influenced by ideas from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_programming" title="Functional programming" id="mwXw">functional programming</a>, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immutability" title="Immutability" class="mw-redirect" id="mwYA">immutability</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higher-order_function" title="Higher-order function" id="mwYQ">higher-order functions</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_data_type" title="Algebraic data type" id="mwYg">algebraic data types</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattern_matching" title="Pattern matching" id="mwYw">pattern matching</a>. It also supports <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object-oriented_programming" title="Object-oriented programming" id="mwZA">object-oriented programming</a> via structs, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_type" title="Union type" id="mwZQ">enums</a>, traits, and methods. Rust enforces memory safety (i.e., that all <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reference_(computer_science)" title="Reference (computer science)" id="mwZg">references</a> point to valid memory) without a conventional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garbage_collection_(computer_science)" title="Garbage collection (computer science)" id="mwZw">garbage collector</a>; instead, memory safety errors and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_race" title="Data race" class="mw-redirect" id="mwaA">data races</a> are prevented by the "borrow checker", which tracks the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object_lifetime" title="Object lifetime" id="mwaQ">object lifetime</a> of references <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compiler" title="Compiler" id="mwag">at compile time</a>.</p>

<p id="mwaw">Software developer Graydon Hoare created Rust in 2006 while working at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla" title="Mozilla" id="mwbA">Mozilla</a>, which officially sponsored the project in 2009. The first stable release, Rust 1.0, was published in May 2015. The project has been sponsored by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Rust_Foundation" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwbQ">Rust Foundation</a> since February 2021.</p>

<p id="mwbg">Rust has been adopted by many software projects, especially <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_service" title="Web service" id="mwbw">web services</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_software" title="System software" id="mwcA">system software</a>. It has been studied academically and has a growing community of developers.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwcQ" data-mw="{&quot;autoGenerated&quot;:true}"></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwcg" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwcw" aria-labelledby="2006–2009:_Early_years"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2006–2009:_Early_years"><span id="2006.E2.80.932009:_Early_years" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2006–2009: Early years</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: 2006–2009: Early years"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwdA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:MozillaCaliforniaHeadquarters.JPG" class="mw-file-description" id="mwdQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:MozillaCaliforniaHeadquarters.JPG" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/MozillaCaliforniaHeadquarters.JPG/250px-MozillaCaliforniaHeadquarters.JPG" decoding="async" data-file-width="2560" data-file-height="1920" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/MozillaCaliforniaHeadquarters.JPG/500px-MozillaCaliforniaHeadquarters.JPG 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwdg"></a><figcaption id="mwdw">Mozilla Foundation headquarters, 650 Castro Street in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_View,_California" title="Mountain View, California" id="mweA">Mountain View, California</a>, June 2009</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mweQ">Rust began as a personal project by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla" title="Mozilla" id="mweg">Mozilla</a> employee Graydon Hoare in 2006. According to <i id="mwew">MIT Technology Review</i>, he started the project due to his frustration with a broken elevator in his apartment building whose software had crashed,<sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-MITTechReview-24&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwfA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfg">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfw">]</span></span></a></sup> and named the language after the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rust_(fungus)" title="Rust (fungus)" id="mwgA">group of fungi of the same name</a> that is "over-engineered for survival".<sup about="#mwt119" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwgQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgw">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhA">]</span></span></a></sup> During the time period between 2006 and 2009, Rust was not publicized to others at Mozilla and was written in Hoare's free time;<sup about="#mwt122" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwhQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhw">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt111" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwiQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;7:50&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 7:50"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>7:50<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> Hoare began speaking about the language around 2009 after a small group at Mozilla became interested in the project.<sup about="#mwt125" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hoare2010_26-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hoare2010&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hoare2010-26&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Hoare2010-26" id="mwig"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwiw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjA">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Hoare cited languages from the 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s as influences — including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CLU_(programming_language)" title="CLU (programming language)" id="mwjg">CLU</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BETA_(programming_language)" title="BETA (programming language)" id="mwjw">BETA</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mesa_(programming_language)" title="Mesa (programming language)" id="mwkA">Mesa</a>, NIL,<sup about="#mwt112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nil_10-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;nil&quot;,&quot;group&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;html&quot;:&quot;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;refn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Refn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;name&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;nil&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-nil-10" data-mw-group="note" id="mwkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkw">[</span>note 4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlA">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erlang_(programming_language)" title="Erlang (programming language)" id="mwlQ">Erlang</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newsqueak" title="Newsqueak" id="mwlg">Newsqueak</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napier88" title="Napier88" id="mwlw">Napier</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hermes_(programming_language)" title="Hermes (programming language)" id="mwmA">Hermes</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sather" title="Sather" id="mwmQ">Sather</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alef_(programming_language)" title="Alef (programming language)" id="mwmg">Alef</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limbo_(programming_language)" title="Limbo (programming language)" id="mwmw">Limbo</a>.<sup about="#mwt126" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hoare2010_26-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hoare2010&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Hoare2010-26" id="mwnA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwng">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnw">]</span></span></a></sup> He described the language as "technology from the past come to save the future from itself."<sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwog">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwow">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt115" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwpA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;8:17&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 8:17"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>8:17<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup><sup about="#mwt128" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hoare2010_26-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hoare2010&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Hoare2010-26" id="mwpQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwpg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpw">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqA">]</span></span></a></sup> Early Rust developer Manish Goregaokar similarly described Rust as being based on "mostly decades-old research."<sup about="#mwt129" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwqQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqw">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwrQ">During the early years, the Rust <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compiler" title="Compiler" id="mwrg">compiler</a> was written in about 38,000 lines of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCaml" title="OCaml" id="mwrw">OCaml</a>.<sup about="#mwt135" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwsA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwsQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsg">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt130" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwtA" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;15:34&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 15:34"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>15:34<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup><sup about="#mwt138" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-OCamlCompiler_27-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;OCamlCompiler&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-OCamlCompiler-27&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-OCamlCompiler-27" id="mwtQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtw">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuA">]</span></span></a></sup> Early Rust contained several features no longer present today, including explicit <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object-oriented_programming" title="Object-oriented programming" id="mwuQ">object-oriented programming</a> via an <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt131" id="mwug" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;style&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;obj&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;code&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Code&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;obj&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">obj</code> keyword<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwuw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvQ">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt133" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwvw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;10:08&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 10:08"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>10:08<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typestate_analysis" title="Typestate analysis" id="mwwA">typestates</a> system for variable state changes, such as going from uninitialized to initialized.<sup about="#mwt140" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwww">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt134" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwxQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;13:12&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 13:12"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>13:12<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwxg" aria-labelledby="2009–2012:_Mozilla_sponsorship"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2009–2012:_Mozilla_sponsorship"><span id="2009.E2.80.932012:_Mozilla_sponsorship" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2009–2012: Mozilla sponsorship</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: 2009–2012: Mozilla sponsorship"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwxw">Mozilla officially sponsored the Rust project in 2009.<sup about="#mwt141" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwyA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyg">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyw">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brendan_Eich" title="Brendan Eich" id="mwzA">Brendan Eich</a> and other executives, intrigued by the possibility of using Rust for a safe <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser" title="Web browser" id="mwzQ">web browser</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title="Browser engine" id="mwzg">engine</a>, placed engineers on the project including Patrick Walton, Niko Matsakis, Felix Klock, and Manish Goregaokar.<sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwzw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0Q">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0g">]</span></span></a></sup> A conference room taken by the project developers was dubbed "the nerd cave," with a sign placed outside the door.<sup about="#mwt143" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mw0w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1Q">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw1w">During this time period, work had shifted from the initial OCaml compiler to a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-hosting_compiler" title="Self-hosting compiler" class="mw-redirect" id="mw2A">self-hosting compiler</a> (<i id="mw2Q">i.e.</i>, written in Rust) targeting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LLVM" title="LLVM" id="mw2g">LLVM</a>.<sup about="#mwt156" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rust0.1_28-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rust0.1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rust0.1-28&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Rust0.1-28" id="mw2w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw3A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3Q">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt144" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-30" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-30&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;refn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Refn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;The list of Rust compiler versions (referred to as a bootstrapping chain) has history going back to 2012.<ref name=Nelson2022RustConf>{{Cite AV media |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oUIjG-y4zaA |last=Nelson |first=Jynn |title=RustConf 2022 - Bootstrapping: The once and future compiler |publisher=Rust Team |date=2022-08-05 |access-date=2024-10-29 |location=Portland, Oregon |via=YouTube}}</ref>&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-30" data-mw-group="note" id="mw3w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4Q">[</span>note 5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4g">]</span></span></a></sup> The ownership system was in place by 2010.<sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mw4w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5Q">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5g">]</span></span></a></sup> The Rust logo was developed in 2011 based on a bicycle chainring.<sup about="#mwt160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-31&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-31" id="mw5w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6Q">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw6w">Rust 0.1 became the first public release on January 20, 2012<sup about="#mwt163" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rust0.1a_32-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rust0.1a&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rust0.1a-32&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Rust0.1a-32" id="mw7A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw7Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7g">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7w">]</span></span></a></sup> for Windows, Linux, and MacOS.<sup about="#mwt166" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ExtremeTechRust0.1_33-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ExtremeTechRust0.1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ExtremeTechRust0.1-33&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ExtremeTechRust0.1-33" id="mw8A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8g">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8w">]</span></span></a></sup> The early 2010s witnessed increasing involvement from full-time engineers at Mozilla and open source volunteers outside Mozilla.<sup about="#mwt167" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mw9A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9g">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mw-A" aria-labelledby="2012–2015:_Evolution"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2012–2015:_Evolution"><span id="2012.E2.80.932015:_Evolution" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2012–2015: Evolution</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: 2012–2015: Evolution"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw-Q">The years from 2012 to 2015 were marked by substantial changes to the Rust <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_system" title="Type system" id="mw-g">type system</a>.<sup about="#mwt172" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mw-w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw_A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_Q">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt168" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mw_w" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;18:36&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 18:36"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>18:36<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup><sup about="#mwt173" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQI">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQM">]</span></span></a></sup> Memory management through the ownership system was gradually consolidated and expanded. By 2013, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garbage_collection_(computer_science)" title="Garbage collection (computer science)" id="mwAQQ">garbage collector</a> was rarely used, and was removed in favor of the ownership system.<sup about="#mwt174" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAQU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQc">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQg">]</span></span></a></sup> Other features were removed in order to simplify the language, including typestates, the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt169" id="mwAQk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;style&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;pure&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;code&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Code&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;pure&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">pure</code> keyword,<sup about="#mwt177" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-34&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mwAQo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQw">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ0">]</span></span></a></sup> various specialized pointer types, and syntax support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Channel_(programming)" title="Channel (programming)" id="mwAQ4">channels</a>.<sup about="#mwt178" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARE">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt171" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwARM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;22:32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 22:32"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>22:32<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

<p id="mwARQ">According to Steve Klabnik, Rust was influenced during this period by developers coming from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C++" title="C++" id="mwARU">C++</a> (e.g., low-level performance of features), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scripting_language" title="Scripting language" id="mwARY">scripting languages</a> (e.g., Cargo and package management), and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_programming" title="Functional programming" id="mwARc">functional programming</a> (e.g., type systems development).<sup about="#mwt180" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwARg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARo">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt179" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwARw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;30:50&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 30:50"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>30:50<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

<p id="mwAR0">Graydon Hoare stepped down from Rust in 2013.<sup about="#mwt186" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAR4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAR8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASA">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASE">]</span></span></a></sup> After Hoare's departure, it evolved organically under a federated governance structure, with a "core team" of initially six people,<sup about="#mwt187" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwASI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASQ">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt181" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwASY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;21:45&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 21:45"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>21:45<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> and around 30-40 developers total across various other teams.<sup about="#mwt188" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwASc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASk">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt182" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwASs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;22:22&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 22:22"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>22:22<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> A <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Request_for_Comments" title="Request for Comments" id="mwASw">Request for Comments</a> (RFC) process for new language features was added in March 2014.<sup about="#mwt189" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAS0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAS4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS8">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt183" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;33:47&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 33:47"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>33:47<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> The core team would grow to nine people by 2016<sup about="#mwt190" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwATI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATQ">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt184" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;21:45&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 21:45"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>21:45<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> with over 1600 RFCs.<sup about="#mwt191" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwATc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATk">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt185" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwATs" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;34:08&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 34:08"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>34:08<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

<p id="mwATw">According to Andrew Binstock for <i id="mwAT0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dr._Dobb's_Journal" title="Dr. Dobb's Journal" id="mwAT4">Dr. Dobb's Journal</a></i> in January 2014, while Rust was "widely viewed as a remarkably elegant language", adoption slowed because it radically changed from version to version.<sup about="#mwt195" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-35" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-35&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-35" id="mwAT8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUE">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUI">]</span></span></a></sup> Rust development at this time focused on finalizing features for version 1.0 so that it could begin promising <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backward_compatibility" title="Backward compatibility" id="mwAUM">backward compatibility</a>.<sup about="#mwt196" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUY">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt192" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAUg" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;41:26&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 41:26"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>41:26<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

<p id="mwAUk">Six years after Mozilla's sponsorship, Rust 1.0 was published and became the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stable_release" title="Stable release" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAUo">stable release</a> on May 15, 2015.<sup about="#mwt198" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAUs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU0">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU4">]</span></span></a></sup> A year later, the Rust compiler had accumulated over 1,400 contributors, and there were over 5,000 third-party libraries published on the Rust package management website Crates.io.<sup about="#mwt199" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAU8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVE">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt197" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAVM" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;43:15&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 43:15"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>43:15<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwAVQ" aria-labelledby="2015–2020:_Servo_and_early_adoption"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2015–2020:_Servo_and_early_adoption"><span id="2015.E2.80.932020:_Servo_and_early_adoption" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2015–2020: Servo and early adoption</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: 2015–2020: Servo and early adoption"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAVU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Home_page_servo_v0.01.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAVY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Home_page_servo_v0.01.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Home_page_servo_v0.01.png/250px-Home_page_servo_v0.01.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="1855" data-file-height="1056" data-file-type="bitmap" height="142" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Home_page_servo_v0.01.png/500px-Home_page_servo_v0.01.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAVc"></a><figcaption id="mwAVg">Early homepage of Mozilla's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Servo_browser_engine" title="Servo browser engine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAVk">Servo browser engine</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwAVo">The development of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Servo_browser_engine" title="Servo browser engine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAVs">Servo browser engine</a> continued in parallel with Rust, jointly funded by Mozilla and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samsung" title="Samsung" id="mwAVw">Samsung</a>.<sup about="#mwt204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-36&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mwAV0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAV4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAV8">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWA">]</span></span></a></sup> The teams behind the two projects worked in close collaboration; new features in Rust were tested out by the Servo team, and new features in Servo were used to give feedback back to the Rust team.<sup about="#mwt205" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAWE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWM">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt200" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWU" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;5:41&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 5:41"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>5:41<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> The first version of Servo was released in 2016.<sup about="#mwt206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAWY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWg">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWk">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox" title="Firefox" id="mwAWo">Firefox</a> web browser shipped with Rust code as of 2016 (version 45),<sup about="#mwt207" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAWs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW0">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt201" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAW8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;53:30&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 53:30"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>53:30<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup><sup about="#mwt210" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-37" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-37&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-37" id="mwAXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXI">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXM">]</span></span></a></sup> but components of Servo did not appear in Firefox until September 2017 (version 57) as part of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(software)" title="Gecko (software)" id="mwAXQ">Gecko</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(software)#Quantum" title="Gecko (software)" id="mwAXU">Quantum</a> projects.<sup about="#mwt213" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-38&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-38" id="mwAXY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXg">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAXo">Improvements were made to the Rust toolchain ecosystem during the years following 1.0 including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Rustfmt" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwAXs">Rustfmt</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_development_environment" title="Integrated development environment" id="mwAXw">integrated development environment</a> integration,<sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAX0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAX4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX8">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt214" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAYE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;44:56&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 44:56"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>44:56<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> and a regular compiler testing and release cycle.<sup about="#mwt218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-18" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAYI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYQ">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt215" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAYY" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;46:48&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 46:48"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>46:48<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup> Rust's community gained a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_of_conduct" title="Code of conduct" id="mwAYc">code of conduct</a> and an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IRC" title="IRC" id="mwAYg">IRC</a> chat for discussion.<sup about="#mwt219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-19" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAYk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYs">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt216" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAY0" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;50:36&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 50:36"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>50:36<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup></p>

<p id="mwAY4">The earliest known adoption outside of Mozilla was by individual projects at Samsung, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook" title="Facebook" id="mwAY8">Facebook</a> (now <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms" title="Meta Platforms" id="mwAZA">Meta Platforms</a>), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dropbox" title="Dropbox" id="mwAZE">Dropbox</a>, and Tilde, Inc., the company behind <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ember.js" title="Ember.js" id="mwAZI">ember.js</a>.<sup about="#mwt221" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Klabnik2016ACMHistory_25-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Klabnik2016ACMHistory&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Klabnik2016ACMHistory-25" id="mwAZM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZU">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup class="reference nowrap" about="#mwt220" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAZc" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;at&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;55:44&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span title="Location: 55:44"><span typeof="mw:Entity">:</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>55:44<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span></sup><sup about="#mwt222" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZo">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZs">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Web_Services" title="Amazon Web Services" id="mwAZw">Amazon Web Services</a> followed in 2020.<sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAZ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ8">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaA">]</span></span></a></sup> Engineers cited performance, lack of a garbage collector, safety, and pleasantness of working in the language as reasons for the adoption. Amazon developers cited a finding by Portuguese researchers that Rust code used <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energy_efficiency_in_computing" title="Energy efficiency in computing" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAaE">less energy</a> compared to similar code written in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java_(programming_language)" title="Java (programming language)" id="mwAaI">Java</a>.<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAaM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaU">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2017PortugalEnergyStudy_39-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;2017PortugalEnergyStudy&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-2017PortugalEnergyStudy-39&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-2017PortugalEnergyStudy-39" id="mwAac"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAak">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAao">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwAas" aria-labelledby="2020–present:_Mozilla_layoffs_and_Rust_Foundation"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2020–present:_Mozilla_layoffs_and_Rust_Foundation"><span id="2020.E2.80.93present:_Mozilla_layoffs_and_Rust_Foundation" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2020–present: Mozilla layoffs and Rust Foundation</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: 2020–present: Mozilla layoffs and Rust Foundation"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAaw">In August 2020, Mozilla laid off 250 of its 1,000 employees worldwide, as part of a corporate restructuring caused by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic" title="COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwAa0">COVID-19 pandemic</a>.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-40" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-40&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-40" id="mwAa4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAa8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbA">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-41" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-41&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-41" id="mwAbI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbQ">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbU">]</span></span></a></sup> The team behind Servo was disbanded. The event raised concerns about the future of Rust.<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-42" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-42&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-42" id="mwAbY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbg">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbk">]</span></span></a></sup> In the following week, the Rust Core Team acknowledged the severe impact of the layoffs and announced that plans for a Rust foundation were underway. The first goal of the foundation would be to take ownership of all <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trademark" title="Trademark" id="mwAbo">trademarks</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domain_name" title="Domain name" id="mwAbs">domain names</a> and to take financial responsibility for their costs.<sup about="#mwt239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-43" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-43&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-43" id="mwAbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAb0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb4">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAcA">On February 8, 2021, the formation of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Rust_Foundation" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwAcE">Rust Foundation</a> was announced by five founding companies: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Web_Services" title="Amazon Web Services" id="mwAcI">Amazon Web Services</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google" title="Google" id="mwAcM">Google</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huawei" title="Huawei" id="mwAcQ">Huawei</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft" title="Microsoft" id="mwAcU">Microsoft</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla" title="Mozilla" id="mwAcY">Mozilla</a>.<sup about="#mwt242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-44&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwAcc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAck">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAco">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-45&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwAcs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc0">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc4">]</span></span></a></sup> The foundation would provide financial support for Rust developers in the form of grants and server funding.<sup about="#mwt246" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwAc8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdE">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdI">]</span></span></a></sup> In a blog post published on April 6, 2021, Google announced support for Rust within the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Android_Open_Source_Project" title="Android Open Source Project" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAdM">Android Open Source Project</a> as an alternative to C/C++.<sup about="#mwt249" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-46&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdY">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAdg">On November 22, 2021, the Moderation Team, which was responsible for enforcing the community code of conduct, announced their resignation "in protest of the Core Team placing themselves unaccountable to anyone but themselves".<sup about="#mwt252" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-moderation_47-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;moderation&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-moderation-47&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-moderation-47" id="mwAdk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAds">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdw">]</span></span></a></sup> In May 2022, members of the Rust leadership council posted a public response to the incident.<sup about="#mwt255" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-48&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwAd0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAd4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd8">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAeE">The Rust Foundation posted a draft for a new trademark policy on April 6, 2023, which resulted in widespread negative reactions from Rust users and contributors.<sup about="#mwt258" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ApologizesTrademarkPolicy_49-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ApologizesTrademarkPolicy&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ApologizesTrademarkPolicy-49&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ApologizesTrademarkPolicy-49" id="mwAeI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeQ">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeU">]</span></span></a></sup> The trademark policy included rules for how the Rust logo and name could be used.<sup about="#mwt259" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ApologizesTrademarkPolicy_49-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ApologizesTrademarkPolicy&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ApologizesTrademarkPolicy-49" id="mwAeY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAec"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeg">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwAeo" aria-labelledby="Syntax_and_features"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Syntax_and_features">Syntax and features</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Syntax and features"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt260" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAes" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Main&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Main&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rust syntax&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt260" id="mwAew">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rust_syntax" title="Rust syntax">Rust syntax</a></div>
<p id="mwAe0">Rust's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syntax_(programming_languages)" title="Syntax (programming languages)" id="mwAe4">syntax</a> is similar to that of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C_(programming_language)" title="C (programming language)" id="mwAe8">C</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/C++" title="C++" id="mwAfA">C++</a>,<sup about="#mwt267" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-50" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-50&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-50" id="mwAfE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfM">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt268" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_51-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;:4&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-:4-51" id="mwAfU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfc">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfg">]</span></span></a></sup> although many of its features were influenced by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functional_programming" title="Functional programming" id="mwAfk">functional programming</a> languages such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OCaml" title="OCaml" id="mwAfo">OCaml</a>.<sup about="#mwt262" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019263_52-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019263&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019263-52&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;263&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019263-52" id="mwAfs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf0">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf4">]</span></span></a></sup> Hoare has described Rust as targeted at frustrated C++ developers.<sup about="#mwt269" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hoare2010_26-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Hoare2010&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Hoare2010-26" id="mwAf8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgE">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwAgM" aria-labelledby="Hello_World_program"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Hello_World_program">Hello World program</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Hello World program"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAgQ">Below is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/&quot;Hello,_World!&quot;_program" title="&quot;Hello, World!&quot; program" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAgU">"Hello, World!" program</a> in Rust. The <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt270" id="mwAgY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;fn&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;fn&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwAgc">fn</span></code> keyword denotes a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Function_(computer_programming)" title="Function (computer programming)" id="mwAgg">function</a>, and the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt272" id="mwAgk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;println!&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;println!&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="fm" id="mwAgo">println!</span></code> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macro_(computer_science)" title="Macro (computer science)" id="mwAgs">macro</a> (see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Macros" about="#mwt274" typeof="mw:Transclusion" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwAgw" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Section link&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Section_link&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Macros&quot;},&quot;nopage&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;y&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">§<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>Macros</a>) prints the message to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_output" title="Standard output" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAg0">standard output</a>.<sup about="#mwt275" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20195–6_53-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20195–6&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20195–6-53&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;5–6&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20195–6-53" id="mwAg4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAg8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhA">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhE">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statement_(computer_science)" title="Statement (computer science)" id="mwAhI">Statements</a> in Rust are separated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semicolon#Programming" title="Semicolon" id="mwAhM">semicolons</a>.</p>
<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt278" id="mwAhQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    println!(\&quot;Hello, World!\&quot;);\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAhU"><span id="mwAhY"></span><span class="k" id="mwAhc">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwAhg"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwAhk">main</span><span class="p" id="mwAho">()</span><span class="w" id="mwAhs"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAhw">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAh0">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwAh4">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwAh8">(</span><span class="s" id="mwAiA">"Hello, World!"</span><span class="p" id="mwAiE">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwAiI">}</span>
</pre></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwAiM" aria-labelledby="Variables"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Variables">Variables</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Variables"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAiQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variable_(computer_science)" title="Variable (computer science)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAiU">Variables</a> in Rust are defined through the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt279" id="mwAiY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;let&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;let&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kd" id="mwAic">let</span></code> keyword.<sup about="#mwt281" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332_54-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332-54&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332-54" id="mwAig"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAik"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAio">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAis">]</span></span></a></sup> The example below assigns a value to the variable with name <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt284" id="mwAiw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;foo&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;foo&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwAi0">foo</span></code> of type <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt286" id="mwAi4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwAi8">i32</span></code> and outputs its value; the type annotation <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt288" id="mwAjA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;: i32&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;: i32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="p" id="mwAjE">:</span><span class="w" id="mwAjI"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwAjM">i32</span></code> can be omitted.</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt290" id="mwAjQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let foo: i32 = 10;\n    println!(\&quot;The value of foo is {foo}\&quot;);\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAjU"><span id="mwAjY"></span><span class="k" id="mwAjc">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwAjg"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwAjk">main</span><span class="p" id="mwAjo">()</span><span class="w" id="mwAjs"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAjw">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAj0">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwAj4">let</span><span class="w" id="mwAj8"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAkA">foo</span><span class="p" id="mwAkE">:</span><span class="w" id="mwAkI"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwAkM">i32</span><span class="w" id="mwAkQ"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAkU">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAkY"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwAkc">10</span><span class="p" id="mwAkg">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAkk">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwAko">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwAks">(</span><span class="s" id="mwAkw">"The value of foo is {foo}"</span><span class="p" id="mwAk0">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwAk4">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwAk8">Variables are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immutable" title="Immutable" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAlA">immutable</a> by default, unless the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt291" id="mwAlE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;mut&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;mut&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwAlI">mut</span></code> keyword is added.<sup about="#mwt293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332–33_55-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332–33&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332–33-55&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;32-33&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202332–33-55" id="mwAlM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlU">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlY">]</span></span></a></sup> The following example uses <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt296" id="mwAlc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;//&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;//&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="c1" id="mwAlg">//</span></code>, which denotes the start of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comment_(computer_programming)" title="Comment (computer programming)" id="mwAlk">comment</a>.<sup about="#mwt298" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202349–50_56-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202349–50&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202349–50-56&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;49-50&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202349–50-56" id="mwAlo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAls"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlw">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAl0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt301" id="mwAl4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    // This code would not compile without adding \&quot;mut\&quot;.\n    let mut foo = 10;\n    println!(\&quot;The value of foo is {foo}\&quot;);\n    foo = 20;\n    println!(\&quot;The value of foo is {foo}\&quot;);\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAl8"><span id="mwAmA"></span><span class="k" id="mwAmE">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwAmI"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwAmM">main</span><span class="p" id="mwAmQ">()</span><span class="w" id="mwAmU"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAmY">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAmc">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwAmg">// This code would not compile without adding "mut".</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAmk">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwAmo">let</span><span class="w" id="mwAms"> </span><span class="k" id="mwAmw">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwAm0"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAm4">foo</span><span class="w" id="mwAm8"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAnA">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAnE"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwAnI">10</span><span class="p" id="mwAnM">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAnQ">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwAnU">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwAnY">(</span><span class="s" id="mwAnc">"The value of foo is {foo}"</span><span class="p" id="mwAng">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAnk">    </span><span class="n" id="mwAno">foo</span><span class="w" id="mwAns"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAnw">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAn0"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwAn4">20</span><span class="p" id="mwAn8">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAoA">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwAoE">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwAoI">(</span><span class="s" id="mwAoM">"The value of foo is {foo}"</span><span class="p" id="mwAoQ">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwAoU">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwAoY">Multiple <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt302" id="mwAoc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;let&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;let&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kd" id="mwAog">let</span></code> expressions can define multiple variables with the same name, known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variable_shadowing" title="Variable shadowing" id="mwAok">variable shadowing</a>. Variable shadowing allows transforming variables without having to name the variables differently.<sup about="#mwt304" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202334–36_57-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202334–36&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202334–36-57&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;34-36&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202334–36-57" id="mwAoo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAos"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAow">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo0">]</span></span></a></sup> The example below declares a new variable with the same name that is double the original value:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt307" id="mwAo4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let foo = 10;\n    // This will output \&quot;The value of foo is 10\&quot;\n    println!(\&quot;The value of foo is {foo}\&quot;);\n    let foo = foo * 2;\n    // This will output \&quot;The value of foo is 20\&quot;\n    println!(\&quot;The value of foo is {foo}\&quot;);\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAo8"><span id="mwApA"></span><span class="k" id="mwApE">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwApI"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwApM">main</span><span class="p" id="mwApQ">()</span><span class="w" id="mwApU"> </span><span class="p" id="mwApY">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwApc">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwApg">let</span><span class="w" id="mwApk"> </span><span class="n" id="mwApo">foo</span><span class="w" id="mwAps"> </span><span class="o" id="mwApw">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAp0"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwAp4">10</span><span class="p" id="mwAp8">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAqA">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwAqE">// This will output "The value of foo is 10"</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAqI">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwAqM">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwAqQ">(</span><span class="s" id="mwAqU">"The value of foo is {foo}"</span><span class="p" id="mwAqY">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAqc">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwAqg">let</span><span class="w" id="mwAqk"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAqo">foo</span><span class="w" id="mwAqs"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAqw">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAq0"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAq4">foo</span><span class="w" id="mwAq8"> </span><span class="o" id="mwArA">*</span><span class="w" id="mwArE"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwArI">2</span><span class="p" id="mwArM">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwArQ">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwArU">// This will output "The value of foo is 20"</span>
<span class="w" id="mwArY">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwArc">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwArg">(</span><span class="s" id="mwArk">"The value of foo is {foo}"</span><span class="p" id="mwAro">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwArs">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwArw">Variable shadowing is also possible for values of different types. For example, going from a string to its length:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt308" id="mwAr0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let letters = \&quot;abc\&quot;;\n    let letters = letters.len();\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAr4"><span id="mwAr8"></span><span class="k" id="mwAsA">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwAsE"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwAsI">main</span><span class="p" id="mwAsM">()</span><span class="w" id="mwAsQ"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAsU">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAsY">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwAsc">let</span><span class="w" id="mwAsg"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAsk">letters</span><span class="w" id="mwAso"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAss">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAsw"> </span><span class="s" id="mwAs0">"abc"</span><span class="p" id="mwAs4">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAs8">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwAtA">let</span><span class="w" id="mwAtE"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAtI">letters</span><span class="w" id="mwAtM"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAtQ">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAtU"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAtY">letters</span><span class="p" id="mwAtc">.</span><span class="n" id="mwAtg">len</span><span class="p" id="mwAtk">();</span>
<span class="p" id="mwAto">}</span>
</pre></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwAts" aria-labelledby="Block_expressions_and_control_flow"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Block_expressions_and_control_flow">Block expressions and control flow</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Block expressions and control flow"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAtw">A <i id="mwAt0">block expression</i> is delimited by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bracket#Curly_brackets" title="Bracket" id="mwAt4">curly brackets</a>. When the last expression inside a block does not end with a semicolon, the block evaluates to the value of that trailing expression:<sup about="#mwt309" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20236,_47,_53_58-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20236, 47, 53&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20236,_47,_53-58&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;6,47,53&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20236,_47,_53-58" id="mwAt8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuE">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt312" id="mwAuM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let x = {\n        println!(\&quot;this is inside the block\&quot;);\n        1 + 2\n    };\n    println!(\&quot;1 + 2 = {x}\&quot;);\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAuQ"><span id="mwAuU"></span><span class="k" id="mwAuY">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwAuc"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwAug">main</span><span class="p" id="mwAuk">()</span><span class="w" id="mwAuo"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAus">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAuw">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwAu0">let</span><span class="w" id="mwAu4"> </span><span class="n" id="mwAu8">x</span><span class="w" id="mwAvA"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAvE">=</span><span class="w" id="mwAvI"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAvM">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAvQ">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwAvU">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwAvY">(</span><span class="s" id="mwAvc">"this is inside the block"</span><span class="p" id="mwAvg">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAvk">        </span><span class="mi" id="mwAvo">1</span><span class="w" id="mwAvs"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAvw">+</span><span class="w" id="mwAv0"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwAv4">2</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAv8">    </span><span class="p" id="mwAwA">};</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAwE">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwAwI">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwAwM">(</span><span class="s" id="mwAwQ">"1 + 2 = {x}"</span><span class="p" id="mwAwU">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwAwY">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwAwc">Trailing expressions of function bodies are used as the return value:<sup about="#mwt313" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202347–48_59-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202347–48&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202347–48-59&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;47-48&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202347–48-59" id="mwAwg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwo">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAws">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt316" id="mwAww" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn add_two(x: i32) -> i32 {\n    x + 2\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAw0"><span id="mwAw4"></span><span class="k" id="mwAw8">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwAxA"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwAxE">add_two</span><span class="p" id="mwAxI">(</span><span class="n" id="mwAxM">x</span><span class="p" id="mwAxQ">:</span><span class="w" id="mwAxU"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwAxY">i32</span><span class="p" id="mwAxc">)</span><span class="w" id="mwAxg"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAxk">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwAxo"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwAxs">i32</span><span class="w" id="mwAxw"> </span><span class="p" id="mwAx0">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwAx4">    </span><span class="n" id="mwAx8">x</span><span class="w" id="mwAyA"> </span><span class="o" id="mwAyE">+</span><span class="w" id="mwAyI"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwAyM">2</span>
<span class="p" id="mwAyQ">}</span>
</pre></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwAyU" aria-labelledby="if_expressions"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="if_expressions"><code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt317" id="mwAyY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;if&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;if&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwAyc">if</span></code> expressions</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: if expressions"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAyg">An <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt319" id="mwAyk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;if&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;if&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwAyo">if</span></code> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conditional_expression" title="Conditional expression" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAys">conditional expression</a> executes code based on whether the given value is <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt321" id="mwAyw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;true&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;true&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kc" id="mwAy0">true</span></code>. <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt323" id="mwAy4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;else&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;else&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwAy8">else</span></code> can be used for when the value evaluates to <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt325" id="mwAzA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;false&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;false&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kc" id="mwAzE">false</span></code>, and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt327" id="mwAzI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;else if&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;else if&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwAzM">else</span><span class="w" id="mwAzQ"> </span><span class="k" id="mwAzU">if</span></code> can be used for combining multiple expressions.<sup about="#mwt329" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53_60-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53-60&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;50-53&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53-60" id="mwAzY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzg">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt332" id="mwAzo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let x = 10;\n    if x > 5 {\n        println!(\&quot;value is greater than five\&quot;);\n    }\n\n    if x % 7 == 0 {\n        println!(\&quot;value is divisible by 7\&quot;);\n    } else if x % 5 == 0 {\n        println!(\&quot;value is divisible by 5\&quot;);\n    } else {\n        println!(\&quot;value is not divisible by 7 or 5\&quot;);\n    }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwAzs"><span id="mwAzw"></span><span class="k" id="mwAz0">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwAz4"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwAz8">main</span><span class="p" id="mwA0A">()</span><span class="w" id="mwA0E"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA0I">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA0M">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwA0Q">let</span><span class="w" id="mwA0U"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA0Y">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA0c"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA0g">=</span><span class="w" id="mwA0k"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA0o">10</span><span class="p" id="mwA0s">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA0w">    </span><span class="k" id="mwA00">if</span><span class="w" id="mwA04"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA08">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA1A"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA1E">&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwA1I"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA1M">5</span><span class="w" id="mwA1Q"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA1U">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA1Y">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwA1c">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwA1g">(</span><span class="s" id="mwA1k">"value is greater than five"</span><span class="p" id="mwA1o">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA1s">    </span><span class="p" id="mwA1w">}</span>

<span class="w" id="mwA10">    </span><span class="k" id="mwA14">if</span><span class="w" id="mwA18"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA2A">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA2E"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA2I">%</span><span class="w" id="mwA2M"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA2Q">7</span><span class="w" id="mwA2U"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA2Y">==</span><span class="w" id="mwA2c"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA2g">0</span><span class="w" id="mwA2k"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA2o">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA2s">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwA2w">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwA20">(</span><span class="s" id="mwA24">"value is divisible by 7"</span><span class="p" id="mwA28">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA3A">    </span><span class="p" id="mwA3E">}</span><span class="w" id="mwA3I"> </span><span class="k" id="mwA3M">else</span><span class="w" id="mwA3Q"> </span><span class="k" id="mwA3U">if</span><span class="w" id="mwA3Y"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA3c">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA3g"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA3k">%</span><span class="w" id="mwA3o"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA3s">5</span><span class="w" id="mwA3w"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA30">==</span><span class="w" id="mwA34"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA38">0</span><span class="w" id="mwA4A"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA4E">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA4I">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwA4M">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwA4Q">(</span><span class="s" id="mwA4U">"value is divisible by 5"</span><span class="p" id="mwA4Y">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA4c">    </span><span class="p" id="mwA4g">}</span><span class="w" id="mwA4k"> </span><span class="k" id="mwA4o">else</span><span class="w" id="mwA4s"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA4w">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA40">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwA44">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwA48">(</span><span class="s" id="mwA5A">"value is not divisible by 7 or 5"</span><span class="p" id="mwA5E">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA5I">    </span><span class="p" id="mwA5M">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwA5Q">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwA5U"><code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt333" id="mwA5Y" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;if&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;if&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwA5c">if</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt335" id="mwA5g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;else&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;else&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwA5k">else</span></code> blocks can evaluate to a value, which can then be assigned to a variable:<sup about="#mwt337" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53_60-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53-60&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;50-53&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202350–53-60" id="mwA5o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA5s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA5w">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA50">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt340" id="mwA54" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let x = 10;\n    let new_x = if x % 2 == 0 { x / 2 } else { 3 * x + 1 };\n    println!(\&quot;{new_x}\&quot;);\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwA58"><span id="mwA6A"></span><span class="k" id="mwA6E">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwA6I"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwA6M">main</span><span class="p" id="mwA6Q">()</span><span class="w" id="mwA6U"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA6Y">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA6c">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwA6g">let</span><span class="w" id="mwA6k"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA6o">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA6s"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA6w">=</span><span class="w" id="mwA60"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA64">10</span><span class="p" id="mwA68">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA7A">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwA7E">let</span><span class="w" id="mwA7I"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA7M">new_x</span><span class="w" id="mwA7Q"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA7U">=</span><span class="w" id="mwA7Y"> </span><span class="k" id="mwA7c">if</span><span class="w" id="mwA7g"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA7k">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA7o"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA7s">%</span><span class="w" id="mwA7w"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA70">2</span><span class="w" id="mwA74"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA78">==</span><span class="w" id="mwA8A"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA8E">0</span><span class="w" id="mwA8I"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA8M">{</span><span class="w" id="mwA8Q"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA8U">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA8Y"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA8c">/</span><span class="w" id="mwA8g"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA8k">2</span><span class="w" id="mwA8o"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA8s">}</span><span class="w" id="mwA8w"> </span><span class="k" id="mwA80">else</span><span class="w" id="mwA84"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA88">{</span><span class="w" id="mwA9A"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA9E">3</span><span class="w" id="mwA9I"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA9M">*</span><span class="w" id="mwA9Q"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA9U">x</span><span class="w" id="mwA9Y"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA9c">+</span><span class="w" id="mwA9g"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwA9k">1</span><span class="w" id="mwA9o"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA9s">};</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA9w">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwA90">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwA94">(</span><span class="s" id="mwA98">"{new_x}"</span><span class="p" id="mwA-A">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwA-E">}</span>
</pre></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwA-I" aria-labelledby="while_loops"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="while_loops"><code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt341" id="mwA-M" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;while&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;while&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwA-Q">while</span></code> loops</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: while loops"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwA-U"><code id="mwA-Y"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/While_loop" title="While loop" class="mw-redirect" id="mwA-c">while</a></code> can be used to repeat a block of code while a condition is met.<sup about="#mwt343" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202356_61-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202356&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202356-61&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;56&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202356-61" id="mwA-g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA-k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-o">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA-s">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt346" id="mwA-w" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    // Iterate over all integers from 4 to 10\n    let mut value = 4;\n    while value <= 10 {\n         println!(\&quot;value = {value}\&quot;);\n         value += 1;\n    }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwA-0"><span id="mwA-4"></span><span class="k" id="mwA-8">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwA_A"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwA_E">main</span><span class="p" id="mwA_I">()</span><span class="w" id="mwA_M"> </span><span class="p" id="mwA_Q">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA_U">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwA_Y">// Iterate over all integers from 4 to 10</span>
<span class="w" id="mwA_c">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwA_g">let</span><span class="w" id="mwA_k"> </span><span class="k" id="mwA_o">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwA_s"> </span><span class="n" id="mwA_w">value</span><span class="w" id="mwA_0"> </span><span class="o" id="mwA_4">=</span><span class="w" id="mwA_8"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBAA">4</span><span class="p" id="mwBAE">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBAI">    </span><span class="k" id="mwBAM">while</span><span class="w" id="mwBAQ"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBAU">value</span><span class="w" id="mwBAY"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBAc">&lt;=</span><span class="w" id="mwBAg"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBAk">10</span><span class="w" id="mwBAo"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBAs">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBAw">         </span><span class="fm" id="mwBA0">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwBA4">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBA8">"value = {value}"</span><span class="p" id="mwBBA">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBBE">         </span><span class="n" id="mwBBI">value</span><span class="w" id="mwBBM"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBBQ">+=</span><span class="w" id="mwBBU"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBBY">1</span><span class="p" id="mwBBc">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBBg">    </span><span class="p" id="mwBBk">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBBo">}</span>
</pre></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="13" id="mwBBs" aria-labelledby="for_loops_and_iterators"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="for_loops_and_iterators"><code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt347" id="mwBBw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;for&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;for&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBB0">for</span></code> loops and iterators</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13" title="Edit section: for loops and iterators"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBB4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/For_loop" title="For loop" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBB8">For loops</a> in Rust loop over elements of a collection.<sup about="#mwt349" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202357–58_62-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202357–58&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202357–58-62&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;57-58&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202357–58-62" id="mwBCA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBCE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCI">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBCM">]</span></span></a></sup>
<code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt352" id="mwBCQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;for&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;for&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBCU">for</span></code> expressions work over any <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iterator" title="Iterator" id="mwBCY">iterator</a> type.</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt354" id="mwBCc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    // Using `for` with range syntax for the same functionality as above\n    // The syntax 4..=10 means the range from 4 to 10, up to and including 10.\n    for value in 4..=10 {\n        println!(\&quot;value = {value}\&quot;);\n    }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBCg"><span id="mwBCk"></span><span class="k" id="mwBCo">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBCs"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBCw">main</span><span class="p" id="mwBC0">()</span><span class="w" id="mwBC4"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBC8">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBDA">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwBDE">// Using `for` with range syntax for the same functionality as above</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBDI">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwBDM">// The syntax 4..=10 means the range from 4 to 10, up to and including 10.</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBDQ">    </span><span class="k" id="mwBDU">for</span><span class="w" id="mwBDY"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBDc">value</span><span class="w" id="mwBDg"> </span><span class="k" id="mwBDk">in</span><span class="w" id="mwBDo"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBDs">4</span><span class="o" id="mwBDw">..=</span><span class="mi" id="mwBD0">10</span><span class="w" id="mwBD4"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBD8">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBEA">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwBEE">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwBEI">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBEM">"value = {value}"</span><span class="p" id="mwBEQ">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBEU">    </span><span class="p" id="mwBEY">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBEc">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwBEg">In the above code, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt355" id="mwBEk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;4..=10&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;4..=10&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mi" id="mwBEo">4</span><span class="o" id="mwBEs">..=</span><span class="mi" id="mwBEw">10</span></code> is a value of type <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt357" id="mwBE0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Range&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Range&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwBE4">Range</span></code> which implements the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt359" id="mwBE8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Iterator&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Iterator&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="nb" id="mwBFA">Iterator</span></code> trait. The code within the curly braces is applied to each element returned by the iterator.</p>

<p id="mwBFE">Iterators can be combined with functions over iterators like <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt361" id="mwBFI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;map&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;map&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwBFM">map</span></code>, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt363" id="mwBFQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;filter&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;filter&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwBFU">filter</span></code>, and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt365" id="mwBFY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;sum&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sum&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwBFc">sum</span></code>. For example, the following adds up all numbers between 1 and 100 that are multiples of 3:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt367" id="mwBFg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\n(1..=100).filter(|x| x % 3 == 0).sum()                  \n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBFk"><span id="mwBFo"></span><span class="p" id="mwBFs">(</span><span class="mi" id="mwBFw">1</span><span class="o" id="mwBF0">..=</span><span class="mi" id="mwBF4">100</span><span class="p" id="mwBF8">).</span><span class="n" id="mwBGA">filter</span><span class="p" id="mwBGE">(</span><span class="o" id="mwBGI">|</span><span class="n" id="mwBGM">x</span><span class="o" id="mwBGQ">|</span><span class="w" id="mwBGU"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBGY">x</span><span class="w" id="mwBGc"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBGg">%</span><span class="w" id="mwBGk"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBGo">3</span><span class="w" id="mwBGs"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBGw">==</span><span class="w" id="mwBG0"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBG4">0</span><span class="p" id="mwBG8">).</span><span class="n" id="mwBHA">sum</span><span class="p" id="mwBHE">()</span>
</pre></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="14" id="mwBHI" aria-labelledby="loop_and_break_statements"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="loop_and_break_statements"><code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt368" id="mwBHM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;loop&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;loop&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBHQ">loop</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt370" id="mwBHU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;break&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;break&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBHY">break</span></code> statements</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14" title="Edit section: loop and break statements"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBHc">More generally, the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt372" id="mwBHg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;loop&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;loop&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBHk">loop</span></code> keyword allows repeating a portion of code until a <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt374" id="mwBHo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;break&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;break&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBHs">break</span></code> occurs. <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt376" id="mwBHw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;break&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;break&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBH0">break</span></code> may optionally exit the loop with a value. In the case of nested loops, labels denoted by <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt378" id="mwBH4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;'label_name&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'label_name&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwBH8">'</span><span class="na" id="mwBIA">label_name</span></code> can be used to break an outer loop rather than the innermost loop.<sup about="#mwt380" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202354–56_63-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202354–56&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202354–56-63&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;54-56&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202354–56-63" id="mwBIE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBII"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIM">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBIQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt383" id="mwBIU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let value = 456;\n    let mut x = 1;\n    let y = loop {\n        x *= 10;\n        if x > value {\n            break x / 10;\n        }\n    };\n    println!(\&quot;largest power of ten that is smaller than or equal to value: {y}\&quot;);\n\n    let mut up = 1;\n    'outer: loop {\n        let mut down = 120;\n        loop {\n            if up > 100 {\n                break 'outer;\n            }\n\n            if down < 4 {\n                break;\n            }\n\n            down /= 2;\n            up += 1;\n            println!(\&quot;up: {up}, down: {down}\&quot;);\n        }\n        up *= 2;\n    }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBIY"><span id="mwBIc"></span><span class="k" id="mwBIg">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBIk"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBIo">main</span><span class="p" id="mwBIs">()</span><span class="w" id="mwBIw"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBI0">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBI4">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwBI8">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBJA"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBJE">value</span><span class="w" id="mwBJI"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBJM">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBJQ"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBJU">456</span><span class="p" id="mwBJY">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBJc">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwBJg">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBJk"> </span><span class="k" id="mwBJo">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwBJs"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBJw">x</span><span class="w" id="mwBJ0"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBJ4">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBJ8"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBKA">1</span><span class="p" id="mwBKE">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBKI">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwBKM">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBKQ"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBKU">y</span><span class="w" id="mwBKY"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBKc">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBKg"> </span><span class="k" id="mwBKk">loop</span><span class="w" id="mwBKo"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBKs">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBKw">        </span><span class="n" id="mwBK0">x</span><span class="w" id="mwBK4"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBK8">*=</span><span class="w" id="mwBLA"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBLE">10</span><span class="p" id="mwBLI">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBLM">        </span><span class="k" id="mwBLQ">if</span><span class="w" id="mwBLU"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBLY">x</span><span class="w" id="mwBLc"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBLg">&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwBLk"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBLo">value</span><span class="w" id="mwBLs"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBLw">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBL0">            </span><span class="k" id="mwBL4">break</span><span class="w" id="mwBL8"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBMA">x</span><span class="w" id="mwBME"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBMI">/</span><span class="w" id="mwBMM"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBMQ">10</span><span class="p" id="mwBMU">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBMY">        </span><span class="p" id="mwBMc">}</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBMg">    </span><span class="p" id="mwBMk">};</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBMo">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwBMs">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwBMw">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBM0">"largest power of ten that is smaller than or equal to value: {y}"</span><span class="p" id="mwBM4">);</span>

<span class="w" id="mwBM8">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwBNA">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBNE"> </span><span class="k" id="mwBNI">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwBNM"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBNQ">up</span><span class="w" id="mwBNU"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBNY">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBNc"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBNg">1</span><span class="p" id="mwBNk">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBNo">    </span><span class="o" id="mwBNs">'</span><span class="na" id="mwBNw">outer</span><span class="p" id="mwBN0">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBN4"> </span><span class="nc" id="mwBN8">loop</span><span class="w" id="mwBOA"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBOE">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBOI">        </span><span class="kd" id="mwBOM">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBOQ"> </span><span class="k" id="mwBOU">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwBOY"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBOc">down</span><span class="w" id="mwBOg"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBOk">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBOo"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBOs">120</span><span class="p" id="mwBOw">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBO0">        </span><span class="k" id="mwBO4">loop</span><span class="w" id="mwBO8"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBPA">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBPE">            </span><span class="k" id="mwBPI">if</span><span class="w" id="mwBPM"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBPQ">up</span><span class="w" id="mwBPU"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBPY">&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwBPc"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBPg">100</span><span class="w" id="mwBPk"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBPo">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBPs">                </span><span class="k" id="mwBPw">break</span><span class="w" id="mwBP0"> </span><span class="nl" id="mwBP4">'outer</span><span class="p" id="mwBP8">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBQA">            </span><span class="p" id="mwBQE">}</span>

<span class="w" id="mwBQI">            </span><span class="k" id="mwBQM">if</span><span class="w" id="mwBQQ"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBQU">down</span><span class="w" id="mwBQY"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBQc">&lt;</span><span class="w" id="mwBQg"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBQk">4</span><span class="w" id="mwBQo"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBQs">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBQw">                </span><span class="k" id="mwBQ0">break</span><span class="p" id="mwBQ4">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBQ8">            </span><span class="p" id="mwBRA">}</span>

<span class="w" id="mwBRE">            </span><span class="n" id="mwBRI">down</span><span class="w" id="mwBRM"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBRQ">/=</span><span class="w" id="mwBRU"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBRY">2</span><span class="p" id="mwBRc">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBRg">            </span><span class="n" id="mwBRk">up</span><span class="w" id="mwBRo"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBRs">+=</span><span class="w" id="mwBRw"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBR0">1</span><span class="p" id="mwBR4">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBR8">            </span><span class="fm" id="mwBSA">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwBSE">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBSI">"up: {up}, down: {down}"</span><span class="p" id="mwBSM">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBSQ">        </span><span class="p" id="mwBSU">}</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBSY">        </span><span class="n" id="mwBSc">up</span><span class="w" id="mwBSg"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBSk">*=</span><span class="w" id="mwBSo"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBSs">2</span><span class="p" id="mwBSw">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBS0">    </span><span class="p" id="mwBS4">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBS8">}</span>
</pre></div>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="15" id="mwBTA" aria-labelledby="Pattern_matching"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Pattern_matching">Pattern matching</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15" title="Edit section: Pattern matching"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBTE">The <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt384" id="mwBTI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;match&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;match&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBTM">match</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt386" id="mwBTQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;if let&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;if let&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBTU">if</span><span class="w" id="mwBTY"> </span><span class="kd" id="mwBTc">let</span></code> expressions can be used for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattern_matching" title="Pattern matching" id="mwBTg">pattern matching</a>. For example, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt388" id="mwBTk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;match&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;match&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBTo">match</span></code> can be used to double an optional integer value if present, and return zero otherwise:<sup about="#mwt390" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019104–109_64-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019104–109&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019104–109-64&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;104–109&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019104–109-64" id="mwBTs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBTw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT0">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBT4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt393" id="mwBT8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn double(x: Option<u64>) -> u64 {\n    match x {\n        Some(y) => y * 2,\n        None => 0,\n    }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBUA"><span id="mwBUE"></span><span class="k" id="mwBUI">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBUM"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBUQ">double</span><span class="p" id="mwBUU">(</span><span class="n" id="mwBUY">x</span><span class="p" id="mwBUc">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBUg"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwBUk">Option</span><span class="o" id="mwBUo">&lt;</span><span class="kt" id="mwBUs">u64</span><span class="o" id="mwBUw">&gt;</span><span class="p" id="mwBU0">)</span><span class="w" id="mwBU4"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBU8">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwBVA"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwBVE">u64</span><span class="w" id="mwBVI"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBVM">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBVQ">    </span><span class="k" id="mwBVU">match</span><span class="w" id="mwBVY"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBVc">x</span><span class="w" id="mwBVg"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBVk">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBVo">        </span><span class="nb" id="mwBVs">Some</span><span class="p" id="mwBVw">(</span><span class="n" id="mwBV0">y</span><span class="p" id="mwBV4">)</span><span class="w" id="mwBV8"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBWA">=&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwBWE"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBWI">y</span><span class="w" id="mwBWM"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBWQ">*</span><span class="w" id="mwBWU"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBWY">2</span><span class="p" id="mwBWc">,</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBWg">        </span><span class="nb" id="mwBWk">None</span><span class="w" id="mwBWo"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBWs">=&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwBWw"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBW0">0</span><span class="p" id="mwBW4">,</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBW8">    </span><span class="p" id="mwBXA">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBXE">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwBXI">Equivalently, this can be written with <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt394" id="mwBXM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;if let&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;if let&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBXQ">if</span><span class="w" id="mwBXU"> </span><span class="kd" id="mwBXY">let</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt396" id="mwBXc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;else&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;else&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwBXg">else</span></code>:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt398" id="mwBXk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn double(x: Option<u64>) -> u64 {\n    if let Some(y) = x {\n        y * 2\n    } else {\n        0\n    }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBXo"><span id="mwBXs"></span><span class="k" id="mwBXw">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBX0"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBX4">double</span><span class="p" id="mwBX8">(</span><span class="n" id="mwBYA">x</span><span class="p" id="mwBYE">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBYI"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwBYM">Option</span><span class="o" id="mwBYQ">&lt;</span><span class="kt" id="mwBYU">u64</span><span class="o" id="mwBYY">&gt;</span><span class="p" id="mwBYc">)</span><span class="w" id="mwBYg"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBYk">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwBYo"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwBYs">u64</span><span class="w" id="mwBYw"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBY0">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBY4">    </span><span class="k" id="mwBY8">if</span><span class="w" id="mwBZA"> </span><span class="kd" id="mwBZE">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBZI"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwBZM">Some</span><span class="p" id="mwBZQ">(</span><span class="n" id="mwBZU">y</span><span class="p" id="mwBZY">)</span><span class="w" id="mwBZc"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBZg">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBZk"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBZo">x</span><span class="w" id="mwBZs"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBZw">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBZ0">        </span><span class="n" id="mwBZ4">y</span><span class="w" id="mwBZ8"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBaA">*</span><span class="w" id="mwBaE"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBaI">2</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBaM">    </span><span class="p" id="mwBaQ">}</span><span class="w" id="mwBaU"> </span><span class="k" id="mwBaY">else</span><span class="w" id="mwBac"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBag">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBak">        </span><span class="mi" id="mwBao">0</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBas">    </span><span class="p" id="mwBaw">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBa0">}</span>
</pre></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="16" id="mwBa4" aria-labelledby="Types"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Types">Types</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16" title="Edit section: Types"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBa8">Rust is <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strongly_typed" title="Strongly typed" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBbA">strongly typed</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statically_typed" title="Statically typed" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBbE">statically typed</a>, meaning that the types of all variables must be known at compilation time. Assigning a value of a particular type to a differently typed variable causes a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compilation_error" title="Compilation error" id="mwBbI">compilation error</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_inference" title="Type inference" id="mwBbM">Type inference</a> is used to determine the type of variables if unspecified.<sup about="#mwt399" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201924_65-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201924&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201924-65&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;24&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201924-65" id="mwBbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBbU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbY">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBbc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBbg">The type <code id="mwBbk">()</code>, called the "unit type" in Rust, is a concrete type that has exactly one value. It occupies no memory (as it represents the absence of value). All functions that do not have an indicated return type implicitly return <code id="mwBbo">()</code>. It is similar to <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-cpp mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt402" id="mwBbs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;cpp&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;void&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cpp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cpp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;void&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBbw">void</span></code><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_example_C++_code" about="#mwt402" id="mwBb0"> in other C-style languages; however, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-cpp mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt404" id="mwBb4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;cpp&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;void&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cpp&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Cpp&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;void&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBb8">void</span></code><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_example_C++_code" about="#mwt404" id="mwBcA"> denotes the absence of a type and cannot have any value.</p>

<p id="mwBcE">The default integer type is <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt406" id="mwBcI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBcM">i32</span></code>, and the default <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floating_point" title="Floating point" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBcQ">floating point</a> type is <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt408" id="mwBcU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;f64&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;f64&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBcY">f64</span></code>. If the type of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Literal_(computer_programming)" title="Literal (computer programming)" id="mwBcc">literal</a> number is not explicitly provided, it is either inferred from the context or the default type is used.<sup about="#mwt410" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201936–38_66-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201936–38&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201936–38-66&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;36–38&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201936–38-66" id="mwBcg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBck"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBco">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBcs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="17" id="mwBcw" aria-labelledby="Primitive_types"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Primitive_types">Primitive types</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17" title="Edit section: Primitive types"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBc0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integer_type" title="Integer type" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBc4">Integer types</a> in Rust are named based on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Signedness" title="Signedness" id="mwBc8">signedness</a> and the number of bits the type takes. For example, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt413" id="mwBdA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBdE">i32</span></code> is a signed integer that takes 32 bits of storage, whereas <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt415" id="mwBdI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;u8&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;u8&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBdM">u8</span></code> is unsigned and only takes 8 bits of storage. <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt417" id="mwBdQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;isize&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;isize&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBdU">isize</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt419" id="mwBdY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;usize&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;usize&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBdc">usize</span></code> take storage depending on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bus_(computing)#Address_bus" title="Bus (computing)" id="mwBdg">memory address bus width</a> of the compilation target. For example, when building for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/32-bit_computing" title="32-bit computing" id="mwBdk">32-bit targets</a>, both types will take up 32 bits of space.<sup about="#mwt423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-67" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-67&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-67" id="mwBdo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBds"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBdw">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBd0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt426" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-68&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwBd4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBd8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeA">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBeE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBeI">By default, integer literals are in base-10, but different <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radix" title="Radix" id="mwBeM">radices</a> are supported with prefixes, for example, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt427" id="mwBeQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;0b11&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;0b11&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mb" id="mwBeU">0b11</span></code> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Binary_number" title="Binary number" id="mwBeY">binary numbers</a>, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt429" id="mwBec" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;0o567&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;0o567&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mo" id="mwBeg">0o567</span></code> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Octal" title="Octal" id="mwBek">octals</a>, and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt431" id="mwBeo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;0xDB&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;0xDB&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mh" id="mwBes">0xDB</span></code> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hexadecimal" title="Hexadecimal" id="mwBew">hexadecimals</a>. By default, integer literals default to <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt433" id="mwBe0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;i32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBe4">i32</span></code> as its type. Suffixes such as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt435" id="mwBe8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;4u32&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;4u32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mi" id="mwBfA">4</span><span class="k" id="mwBfE">u32</span></code> can be used to explicitly set the type of a literal.<sup about="#mwt437" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202336–38_69-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202336–38&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202336–38-69&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;36-38&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202336–38-69" id="mwBfI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfQ">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBfU">]</span></span></a></sup> Byte literals such as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt440" id="mwBfY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;b'X'&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;b'X'&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="sc" id="mwBfc">b'X'</span></code> are available to represent the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ASCII" title="ASCII" id="mwBfg">ASCII</a> value (as a <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt442" id="mwBfk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;u8&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;u8&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBfo">u8</span></code>) of a specific character.<sup about="#mwt444" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023502_70-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023502&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023502-70&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;502&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023502-70" id="mwBfs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBf0">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBf4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBf8">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boolean_type" title="Boolean type" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBgA">Boolean type</a> is referred to as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt447" id="mwBgE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;bool&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;bool&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBgI">bool</span></code> which can take a value of either <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt449" id="mwBgM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;true&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;true&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kc" id="mwBgQ">true</span></code> or <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt451" id="mwBgU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;false&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;false&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kc" id="mwBgY">false</span></code>. A <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt453" id="mwBgc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;char&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;char&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBgg">char</span></code> takes up 32 bits of space and represents a Unicode scalar value:<sup about="#mwt464" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-71" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-71&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-71" id="mwBgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgs">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBgw">]</span></span></a></sup> a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unicode_codepoint" title="Unicode codepoint" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBg0">Unicode codepoint</a> that is not a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_Character_Set_characters#Surrogates" title="Universal Character Set characters" id="mwBg4">surrogate</a>.<sup about="#mwt467" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-72&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-72" id="mwBg8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhE">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhI">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IEEE_754" title="IEEE 754" id="mwBhM">IEEE 754</a> floating point numbers are supported with <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt455" id="mwBhQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;f32&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;f32&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBhU">f32</span></code> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_precision_float" title="Single precision float" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBhY">single precision floats</a> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt457" id="mwBhc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;f64&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;f64&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="kt" id="mwBhg">f64</span></code> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_precision_float" title="Double precision float" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBhk">double precision floats</a>.<sup about="#mwt459" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201938–40_73-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201938–40&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201938–40-73&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;38–40&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201938–40-73" id="mwBho"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBhs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBhw">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBh0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="18" id="mwBh4" aria-labelledby="Compound_types"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Compound_types">Compound types</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18" title="Edit section: Compound types"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBh8">Compound types can contain multiple values. Tuples are fixed-size lists that can contain values whose types can be different. Arrays are fixed-size lists whose values are of the same type. Expressions of the tuple and array types can be written through listing the values, and can be accessed with <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt468" id="mwBiA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;.index&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;.index&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="p" id="mwBiE">.</span><span class="n" id="mwBiI">index</span></code> (with tuples) or <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt470" id="mwBiM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;[index]&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[index]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="p" id="mwBiQ">[</span><span class="n" id="mwBiU">index</span><span class="p" id="mwBiY">]</span></code> (with arrays):<sup about="#mwt472" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202340–42_74-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202340–42&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202340–42-74&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;40-42&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202340–42-74" id="mwBic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBik">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBio">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt475" id="mwBis" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nlet tuple: (u32, bool) = (3, true);\nlet array: [i8; 5] = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];\nlet value = tuple.1; // true\nlet value = array[2]; // 3\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBiw"><span id="mwBi0"></span><span class="kd" id="mwBi4">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBi8"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBjA">tuple</span><span class="p" id="mwBjE">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBjI"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBjM">(</span><span class="kt" id="mwBjQ">u32</span><span class="p" id="mwBjU">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBjY"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwBjc">bool</span><span class="p" id="mwBjg">)</span><span class="w" id="mwBjk"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBjo">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBjs"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBjw">(</span><span class="mi" id="mwBj0">3</span><span class="p" id="mwBj4">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBj8"> </span><span class="kc" id="mwBkA">true</span><span class="p" id="mwBkE">);</span>
<span class="kd" id="mwBkI">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBkM"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBkQ">array</span><span class="p" id="mwBkU">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBkY"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBkc">[</span><span class="kt" id="mwBkg">i8</span><span class="p" id="mwBkk">;</span><span class="w" id="mwBko"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBks">5</span><span class="p" id="mwBkw">]</span><span class="w" id="mwBk0"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBk4">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBk8"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBlA">[</span><span class="mi" id="mwBlE">1</span><span class="p" id="mwBlI">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBlM"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBlQ">2</span><span class="p" id="mwBlU">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBlY"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBlc">3</span><span class="p" id="mwBlg">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBlk"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBlo">4</span><span class="p" id="mwBls">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBlw"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBl0">5</span><span class="p" id="mwBl4">];</span>
<span class="kd" id="mwBl8">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBmA"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBmE">value</span><span class="w" id="mwBmI"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBmM">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBmQ"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBmU">tuple</span><span class="p" id="mwBmY">.</span><span class="mi" id="mwBmc">1</span><span class="p" id="mwBmg">;</span><span class="w" id="mwBmk"> </span><span class="c1" id="mwBmo">// true</span>
<span class="kd" id="mwBms">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBmw"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBm0">value</span><span class="w" id="mwBm4"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBm8">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBnA"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBnE">array</span><span class="p" id="mwBnI">[</span><span class="mi" id="mwBnM">2</span><span class="p" id="mwBnQ">];</span><span class="w" id="mwBnU"> </span><span class="c1" id="mwBnY">// 3</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwBnc">Arrays can also be constructed through copying a single value a number of times:<sup about="#mwt476" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202342_75-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202342&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202342-75&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;42&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202342-75" id="mwBng"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBno">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBns">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt479" id="mwBnw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nlet array2: [char; 10] = [' '; 10];\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBn0"><span id="mwBn4"></span><span class="kd" id="mwBn8">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBoA"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBoE">array2</span><span class="p" id="mwBoI">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBoM"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBoQ">[</span><span class="kt" id="mwBoU">char</span><span class="p" id="mwBoY">;</span><span class="w" id="mwBoc"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBog">10</span><span class="p" id="mwBok">]</span><span class="w" id="mwBoo"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBos">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBow"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBo0">[</span><span class="sc" id="mwBo4">' '</span><span class="p" id="mwBo8">;</span><span class="w" id="mwBpA"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwBpE">10</span><span class="p" id="mwBpI">];</span>
</pre></div>
<!-- todo str, and ! -->

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="19" id="mwBpM" aria-labelledby="Ownership_and_references"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Ownership_and_references">Ownership and references</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19" title="Edit section: Ownership and references"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBpQ">Rust's ownership system consists of rules that ensure memory safety without using a garbage collector. At compile time, each value must be attached to a variable called the <i id="mwBpU">owner</i> of that value, and every value must have exactly one owner.<sup about="#mwt480" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201959–61_76-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201959–61&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201959–61-76&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;59–61&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201959–61-76" id="mwBpY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpg">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpk">]</span></span></a></sup> Values are moved between different owners through assignment or passing a value as a function parameter. Values can also be <i id="mwBpo">borrowed,</i> meaning they are temporarily passed to a different function before being returned to the owner.<sup about="#mwt483" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68_77-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68-77&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;63–68&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68-77" id="mwBps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp0">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp4">]</span></span></a></sup> With these rules, Rust can prevent the creation and use of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dangling_pointers" title="Dangling pointers" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBp8">dangling pointers</a>:<sup about="#mwt486" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68_77-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68-77&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;63–68&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201963–68-77" id="mwBqA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqI">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt489" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201974–75_78-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201974–75&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201974–75-78&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;74–75&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201974–75-78" id="mwBqQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqY">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt492" id="mwBqg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn print_string(s: String) {\n    println!(\&quot;{}\&quot;, s);\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let s = String::from(\&quot;Hello, World\&quot;);\n    print_string(s); // s consumed by print_string\n    // s has been moved, so cannot be used any more\n    // another print_string(s); would result in a compile error\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBqk"><span id="mwBqo"></span><span class="k" id="mwBqs">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBqw"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBq0">print_string</span><span class="p" id="mwBq4">(</span><span class="n" id="mwBq8">s</span><span class="p" id="mwBrA">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBrE"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwBrI">String</span><span class="p" id="mwBrM">)</span><span class="w" id="mwBrQ"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBrU">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBrY">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwBrc">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwBrg">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBrk">"{}"</span><span class="p" id="mwBro">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBrs"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBrw">s</span><span class="p" id="mwBr0">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBr4">}</span>

<span class="k" id="mwBr8">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBsA"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBsE">main</span><span class="p" id="mwBsI">()</span><span class="w" id="mwBsM"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBsQ">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBsU">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwBsY">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBsc"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBsg">s</span><span class="w" id="mwBsk"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBso">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBss"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwBsw">String</span><span class="p" id="mwBs0">::</span><span class="n" id="mwBs4">from</span><span class="p" id="mwBs8">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBtA">"Hello, World"</span><span class="p" id="mwBtE">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBtI">    </span><span class="n" id="mwBtM">print_string</span><span class="p" id="mwBtQ">(</span><span class="n" id="mwBtU">s</span><span class="p" id="mwBtY">);</span><span class="w" id="mwBtc"> </span><span class="c1" id="mwBtg">// s consumed by print_string</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBtk">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwBto">// s has been moved, so cannot be used any more</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBts">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwBtw">// another print_string(s); would result in a compile error</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBt0">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwBt4">The function <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt493" id="mwBt8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;print_string&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;print_string&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwBuA">print_string</span></code> takes ownership over the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt495" id="mwBuE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;String&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;String&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="nb" id="mwBuI">String</span></code> value passed in; Alternatively, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt497" id="mwBuM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&amp;&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&amp;&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwBuQ">&amp;</span></code> can be used to indicate a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reference_(computer_science)" title="Reference (computer science)" id="mwBuU">reference</a> type (in <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt499" id="mwBuY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&amp;String&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&amp;String&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwBuc">&amp;</span><span class="nb" id="mwBug">String</span></code>) and to create a reference (in <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt501" id="mwBuk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&amp;s&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&amp;s&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwBuo">&amp;</span><span class="n" id="mwBus">s</span></code>):<sup about="#mwt503" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202371–72_79-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202371–72&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202371–72-79&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;71–72&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202371–72-79" id="mwBuw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBu0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBu4">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBu8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt506" id="mwBvA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn print_string(s: &amp;String) {\n    println!(\&quot;{}\&quot;, s);\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let s = String::from(\&quot;Hello, World\&quot;);\n    print_string(&amp;s); // s borrowed by print_string\n    print_string(&amp;s); // s has not been consumed; we can call the function many times\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwBvE"><span id="mwBvI"></span><span class="k" id="mwBvM">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBvQ"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBvU">print_string</span><span class="p" id="mwBvY">(</span><span class="n" id="mwBvc">s</span><span class="p" id="mwBvg">:</span><span class="w" id="mwBvk"> </span><span class="kp" id="mwBvo">&amp;</span><span class="nb" id="mwBvs">String</span><span class="p" id="mwBvw">)</span><span class="w" id="mwBv0"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBv4">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBv8">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwBwA">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwBwE">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBwI">"{}"</span><span class="p" id="mwBwM">,</span><span class="w" id="mwBwQ"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBwU">s</span><span class="p" id="mwBwY">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBwc">}</span>

<span class="k" id="mwBwg">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwBwk"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwBwo">main</span><span class="p" id="mwBws">()</span><span class="w" id="mwBww"> </span><span class="p" id="mwBw0">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBw4">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwBw8">let</span><span class="w" id="mwBxA"> </span><span class="n" id="mwBxE">s</span><span class="w" id="mwBxI"> </span><span class="o" id="mwBxM">=</span><span class="w" id="mwBxQ"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwBxU">String</span><span class="p" id="mwBxY">::</span><span class="n" id="mwBxc">from</span><span class="p" id="mwBxg">(</span><span class="s" id="mwBxk">"Hello, World"</span><span class="p" id="mwBxo">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwBxs">    </span><span class="n" id="mwBxw">print_string</span><span class="p" id="mwBx0">(</span><span class="o" id="mwBx4">&amp;</span><span class="n" id="mwBx8">s</span><span class="p" id="mwByA">);</span><span class="w" id="mwByE"> </span><span class="c1" id="mwByI">// s borrowed by print_string</span>
<span class="w" id="mwByM">    </span><span class="n" id="mwByQ">print_string</span><span class="p" id="mwByU">(</span><span class="o" id="mwByY">&amp;</span><span class="n" id="mwByc">s</span><span class="p" id="mwByg">);</span><span class="w" id="mwByk"> </span><span class="c1" id="mwByo">// s has not been consumed; we can call the function many times</span>
<span class="p" id="mwBys">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwByw">Because of these ownership rules, Rust types are known as <i id="mwBy0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Affine_type" title="Affine type" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBy4">affine types</a></i>, meaning each value may be used at most once. This enforces a form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_fault_isolation" title="Software fault isolation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBy8">software fault isolation</a> as the owner of a value is solely responsible for its correctness and deallocation.<sup about="#mwt509" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BeyondSafety_80-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;BeyondSafety&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-BeyondSafety-80&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-BeyondSafety-80" id="mwBzA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzI">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBzM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBzQ">When a value goes out of scope, it is <i id="mwBzU">dropped</i> by running its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destructor_(computer_programming)" title="Destructor (computer programming)" id="mwBzY">destructor</a>. The destructor may be programmatically defined through implementing the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt510" id="mwBzc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Drop&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Drop&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="nb" id="mwBzg">Drop</span></code> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Traits" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwBzk">trait</a>. This helps manage resources such as file handles, network sockets, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lock_(computer_science)" title="Lock (computer science)" id="mwBzo">locks</a>, since when objects are dropped, the resources associated with them are closed or released automatically.<sup about="#mwt512" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023327–30_81-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023327–30&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023327–30-81&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;327-30&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023327–30-81" id="mwBzs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBzw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBz0">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBz4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="20" id="mwBz8" aria-labelledby="Lifetimes"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Lifetimes">Lifetimes</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20" title="Edit section: Lifetimes"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwB0A"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object_lifetime" title="Object lifetime" id="mwB0E">Object lifetime</a> refers to the period of time during which a reference is valid; that is, the time between the object creation and destruction.<sup about="#mwt521" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-82" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-82&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-82" id="mwB0I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB0M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0Q">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB0U">]</span></span></a></sup> These <i id="mwB0Y">lifetimes</i> are implicitly associated with all Rust reference types. While often inferred, they can also be indicated explicitly with named lifetime parameters (often denoted <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt515" id="mwB0c" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;'a&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'a&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwB0g">'</span><span class="na" id="mwB0k">a</span></code>, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt517" id="mwB0o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;'b&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'b&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwB0s">'</span><span class="na" id="mwB0w">b</span></code>, and so on).<sup about="#mwt524" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-83" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-83&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-83" id="mwB00"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB04"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB08">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwB1E">A value's lifetime in Rust is inferred from the set of locations in the source code (i.e., function, line, and column numbers) for which a variable is valid.<sup about="#mwt525" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194_84-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194-84&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;194&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194-84" id="mwB1I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1Q">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1U">]</span></span></a></sup> For example, a reference to a local variable has a lifetime from the expression it is declared in up until the last use of it.<sup about="#mwt528" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194_84-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194-84&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;194&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194-84" id="mwB1Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB1c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1g">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB1k">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt531" id="mwB1o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let mut x = 5;            // ------------------+- Lifetime 'a\n                              //                   |\n    let r = &amp;x;               // -+-- Lifetime 'b  |\n                              //  |                |\n    println!(\&quot;r: {}\&quot;, r);     // -+                |\n    // Since r is no longer used,                  |\n    // its lifetime ends                           |\n    let r2 = &amp;mut x;          // -+-- Lifetime 'c  |\n}                             // ------------------+\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwB1s"><span id="mwB1w"></span><span class="k" id="mwB10">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwB14"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwB18">main</span><span class="p" id="mwB2A">()</span><span class="w" id="mwB2E"> </span><span class="p" id="mwB2I">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB2M">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwB2Q">let</span><span class="w" id="mwB2U"> </span><span class="k" id="mwB2Y">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwB2c"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB2g">x</span><span class="w" id="mwB2k"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB2o">=</span><span class="w" id="mwB2s"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwB2w">5</span><span class="p" id="mwB20">;</span><span class="w" id="mwB24">            </span><span class="c1" id="mwB28">// ------------------+- Lifetime 'a</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB3A">                              </span><span class="c1" id="mwB3E">//                   |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB3I">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwB3M">let</span><span class="w" id="mwB3Q"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB3U">r</span><span class="w" id="mwB3Y"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB3c">=</span><span class="w" id="mwB3g"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB3k">&amp;</span><span class="n" id="mwB3o">x</span><span class="p" id="mwB3s">;</span><span class="w" id="mwB3w">               </span><span class="c1" id="mwB30">// -+-- Lifetime 'b  |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB34">                              </span><span class="c1" id="mwB38">//  |                |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB4A">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwB4E">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwB4I">(</span><span class="s" id="mwB4M">"r: {}"</span><span class="p" id="mwB4Q">,</span><span class="w" id="mwB4U"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB4Y">r</span><span class="p" id="mwB4c">);</span><span class="w" id="mwB4g">     </span><span class="c1" id="mwB4k">// -+                |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB4o">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwB4s">// Since r is no longer used,                  |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB4w">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwB40">// its lifetime ends                           |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB44">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwB48">let</span><span class="w" id="mwB5A"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB5E">r2</span><span class="w" id="mwB5I"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB5M">=</span><span class="w" id="mwB5Q"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB5U">&amp;</span><span class="k" id="mwB5Y">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwB5c"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB5g">x</span><span class="p" id="mwB5k">;</span><span class="w" id="mwB5o">          </span><span class="c1" id="mwB5s">// -+-- Lifetime 'c  |</span>
<span class="p" id="mwB5w">}</span><span class="w" id="mwB50">                             </span><span class="c1" id="mwB54">// ------------------+</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwB58">The borrow checker in the Rust compiler then enforces that references are only used in the locations of the source code where the associated lifetime is valid.<sup about="#mwt532" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201975,_134_85-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201975, 134&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201975,_134-85&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;75,134&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201975,_134-85" id="mwB6A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6I">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6M">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt551" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-86" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-86&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-86" id="mwB6Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB6U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6Y">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB6c">]</span></span></a></sup> In the example above, storing a reference to variable <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt535" id="mwB6g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;x&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;x&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwB6k">x</span></code> in <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt537" id="mwB6o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;r&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;r&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwB6s">r</span></code> is valid, as variable <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt539" id="mwB6w" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;x&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;x&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwB60">x</span></code> has a longer lifetime (<code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt541" id="mwB64" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;'a&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'a&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwB68">'</span><span class="na" id="mwB7A">a</span></code>) than variable <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt543" id="mwB7E" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;r&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;r&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwB7I">r</span></code> (<code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt545" id="mwB7M" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;'b&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'b&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwB7Q">'</span><span class="na" id="mwB7U">b</span></code>). However, when <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt547" id="mwB7Y" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;x&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;x&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwB7c">x</span></code> has a shorter lifetime, the borrow checker would reject the program:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt552" id="mwB7g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let r;                    // ------------------+- Lifetime 'a\n                              //                   |\n    {                         //                   |\n        let x = 5;            // -+-- Lifetime 'b  |\n        r = &amp;x; // ERROR: x does  |                |\n    }           // not live long -|                |\n                // enough                          |\n    println!(\&quot;r: {}\&quot;, r);     //                   |\n}                             // ------------------+\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwB7k"><span id="mwB7o"></span><span class="k" id="mwB7s">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwB7w"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwB70">main</span><span class="p" id="mwB74">()</span><span class="w" id="mwB78"> </span><span class="p" id="mwB8A">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB8E">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwB8I">let</span><span class="w" id="mwB8M"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB8Q">r</span><span class="p" id="mwB8U">;</span><span class="w" id="mwB8Y">                    </span><span class="c1" id="mwB8c">// ------------------+- Lifetime 'a</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB8g">                              </span><span class="c1" id="mwB8k">//                   |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB8o">    </span><span class="p" id="mwB8s">{</span><span class="w" id="mwB8w">                         </span><span class="c1" id="mwB80">//                   |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB84">        </span><span class="kd" id="mwB88">let</span><span class="w" id="mwB9A"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB9E">x</span><span class="w" id="mwB9I"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB9M">=</span><span class="w" id="mwB9Q"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwB9U">5</span><span class="p" id="mwB9Y">;</span><span class="w" id="mwB9c">            </span><span class="c1" id="mwB9g">// -+-- Lifetime 'b  |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB9k">        </span><span class="n" id="mwB9o">r</span><span class="w" id="mwB9s"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB9w">=</span><span class="w" id="mwB90"> </span><span class="o" id="mwB94">&amp;</span><span class="n" id="mwB98">x</span><span class="p" id="mwB-A">;</span><span class="w" id="mwB-E"> </span><span class="c1" id="mwB-I">// ERROR: x does  |                |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB-M">    </span><span class="p" id="mwB-Q">}</span><span class="w" id="mwB-U">           </span><span class="c1" id="mwB-Y">// not live long -|                |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB-c">                </span><span class="c1" id="mwB-g">// enough                          |</span>
<span class="w" id="mwB-k">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwB-o">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwB-s">(</span><span class="s" id="mwB-w">"r: {}"</span><span class="p" id="mwB-0">,</span><span class="w" id="mwB-4"> </span><span class="n" id="mwB-8">r</span><span class="p" id="mwB_A">);</span><span class="w" id="mwB_E">     </span><span class="c1" id="mwB_I">//                   |</span>
<span class="p" id="mwB_M">}</span><span class="w" id="mwB_Q">                             </span><span class="c1" id="mwB_U">// ------------------+</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwB_Y">Since the lifetime of the referenced variable (<code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt553" id="mwB_c" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;'b&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'b&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwB_g">'</span><span class="na" id="mwB_k">b</span></code>) is shorter than the lifetime of the variable holding the reference (<code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt555" id="mwB_o" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;'a&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;'a&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwB_s">'</span><span class="na" id="mwB_w">a</span></code>), the borrow checker errors, preventing <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt557" id="mwB_0" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;x&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;x&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwB_4">x</span></code> from being used from outside its scope.<sup about="#mwt559" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194–195_87-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194–195&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194–195-87&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;194-195&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019194–195-87" id="mwB_8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAE">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCAM">Lifetimes can be indicated using explicit <i id="mwCAQ">lifetime parameters</i> on function arguments. For example, the following code specifies that the reference returned by the function has the same lifetime as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt562" id="mwCAU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;original&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;original&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCAY">original</span></code> (and <i id="mwCAc">not</i> necessarily the same lifetime as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt564" id="mwCAg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;prefix&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;prefix&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCAk">prefix</span></code>):<sup about="#mwt566" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023208–12_88-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023208–12&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023208–12-88&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;208–12&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023208–12-88" id="mwCAo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAw">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt569" id="mwCA4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn remove_prefix<'a>(mut original: &amp;'a str, prefix: &amp;str) -> &amp;'a str {\n    if original.starts_with(prefix) {\n        original = original[prefix.len()..];\n    }\n    original\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwCA8"><span id="mwCBA"></span><span class="k" id="mwCBE">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCBI"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCBM">remove_prefix</span><span class="o" id="mwCBQ">&lt;'</span><span class="na" id="mwCBU">a</span><span class="o" id="mwCBY">&gt;</span><span class="p" id="mwCBc">(</span><span class="k" id="mwCBg">mut</span><span class="w" id="mwCBk"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCBo">original</span><span class="p" id="mwCBs">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCBw"> </span><span class="kp" id="mwCB0">&amp;</span><span class="o" id="mwCB4">'</span><span class="na" id="mwCB8">a</span><span class="w" id="mwCCA"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCCE">str</span><span class="p" id="mwCCI">,</span><span class="w" id="mwCCM"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCCQ">prefix</span><span class="p" id="mwCCU">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCCY"> </span><span class="kp" id="mwCCc">&amp;</span><span class="kt" id="mwCCg">str</span><span class="p" id="mwCCk">)</span><span class="w" id="mwCCo"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCCs">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCCw"> </span><span class="kp" id="mwCC0">&amp;</span><span class="o" id="mwCC4">'</span><span class="na" id="mwCC8">a</span><span class="w" id="mwCDA"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCDE">str</span><span class="w" id="mwCDI"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCDM">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCDQ">    </span><span class="k" id="mwCDU">if</span><span class="w" id="mwCDY"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCDc">original</span><span class="p" id="mwCDg">.</span><span class="n" id="mwCDk">starts_with</span><span class="p" id="mwCDo">(</span><span class="n" id="mwCDs">prefix</span><span class="p" id="mwCDw">)</span><span class="w" id="mwCD0"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCD4">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCD8">        </span><span class="n" id="mwCEA">original</span><span class="w" id="mwCEE"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCEI">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCEM"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCEQ">original</span><span class="p" id="mwCEU">[</span><span class="n" id="mwCEY">prefix</span><span class="p" id="mwCEc">.</span><span class="n" id="mwCEg">len</span><span class="p" id="mwCEk">()</span><span class="o" id="mwCEo">..</span><span class="p" id="mwCEs">];</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCEw">    </span><span class="p" id="mwCE0">}</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCE4">    </span><span class="n" id="mwCE8">original</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCFA">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwCFE">In the compiler, ownership and lifetimes work together to prevent memory safety issues such as dangling pointers.<sup about="#mwt570" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch04-02-references-and-borrowinghtml_4.2._References_and_Borrowing]_89-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch04-02-references-and-borrowinghtml 4.2. References and Borrowing]&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch04-02-references-and-borrowinghtml_4.2._References_and_Borrowing]-89&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch04-02-references-and-borrowing.html 4.2. References and Borrowing]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch04-02-references-and-borrowinghtml_4.2._References_and_Borrowing]-89" id="mwCFI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFQ">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt575" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pearce_90-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Pearce&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pearce-90&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Pearce-90" id="mwCFY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFg">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="21" id="mwCFo" aria-labelledby="User-defined_types"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="User-defined_types">User-defined types</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21" title="Edit section: User-defined types"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCFs">User-defined types are created with the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt576" id="mwCFw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;struct&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;struct&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCF0">struct</span></code> or <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt578" id="mwCF4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;enum&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;enum&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCF8">enum</span></code> keywords. The <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt580" id="mwCGA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;struct&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;struct&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCGE">struct</span></code> keyword is used to denote a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Record_(computer_science)" title="Record (computer science)" id="mwCGI">record type</a> that groups multiple related values.<sup about="#mwt582" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201983_91-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201983&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201983-91&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;83&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201983-91" id="mwCGM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGU">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGY">]</span></span></a></sup> <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt585" id="mwCGc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;enum&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;enum&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCGg">enum</span></code>s can take on different variants at runtime, with their capabilities similar to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_data_types" title="Algebraic data types" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCGk">algebraic data types</a> found in functional programming languages.<sup about="#mwt587" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201997_92-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201997&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201997-92&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;97&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201997-92" id="mwCGo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGw">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCG0">]</span></span></a></sup> Both records and enum variants can contain <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Field_(computer_science)" title="Field (computer science)" id="mwCG4">fields</a> with different types.<sup about="#mwt590" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201998–101_93-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201998–101&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201998–101-93&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;98–101&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201998–101-93" id="mwCG8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHE">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHI">]</span></span></a></sup> Alternative names, or aliases, for the same type can be defined with the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt593" id="mwCHM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;type&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;type&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCHQ">type</span></code> keyword.<sup about="#mwt595" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019438–440_94-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019438–440&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019438–440-94&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;438–440&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019438–440-94" id="mwCHU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHc">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCHk">The <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt598" id="mwCHo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;impl&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;impl&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCHs">impl</span></code> keyword can define methods for a user-defined type. Data and functions are defined separately. Implementations fulfill a role similar to that of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Class_(programming)" title="Class (programming)" id="mwCHw">classes</a> within other languages.<sup about="#mwt600" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201993_95-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201993&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201993-95&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;93&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201993-95" id="mwCH0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCH4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCH8">[</span>90<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwCIE" aria-labelledby="Standard_library"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Standard_library">Standard library</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22" title="Edit section: Standard library"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCII"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rust_standard_libraries.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCIM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rust_standard_libraries.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Rust_standard_libraries.svg/250px-Rust_standard_libraries.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="259" data-file-height="325" data-file-type="drawing" height="314" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Rust_standard_libraries.svg/500px-Rust_standard_libraries.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCIQ"></a><figcaption id="mwCIU">A diagram of the dependencies between the standard library modules of Rust</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCIY">The Rust <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standard_library" title="Standard library" id="mwCIc">standard library</a> defines and implements many widely used custom data types, including core data structures such as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt603" id="mwCIg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Vec&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Vec&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="nb" id="mwCIk">Vec</span></code>, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt605" id="mwCIo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Option&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Option&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="nb" id="mwCIs">Option</span></code>, and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt607" id="mwCIw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;HashMap&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;HashMap&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCI0">HashMap</span></code>, as well as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smart_pointer" title="Smart pointer" id="mwCI4">smart pointer</a> types. Rust provides a way to exclude most of the standard library using the attribute <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt609" id="mwCI8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;#![no_std]&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#![no_std]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="cp" id="mwCJA">#![no_std]</span></code>, for applications such as embedded devices. Internally, the standard library is divided into three parts, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt611" id="mwCJE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;core&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;core&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCJI">core</span></code>, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt613" id="mwCJM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;alloc&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;alloc&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCJQ">alloc</span></code>, and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt615" id="mwCJU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;std&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;std&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCJY">std</span></code>, where <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt617" id="mwCJc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;std&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;std&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCJg">std</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt619" id="mwCJk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;alloc&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;alloc&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCJo">alloc</span></code> are excluded by <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt621" id="mwCJs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;#![no_std]&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#![no_std]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="cp" id="mwCJw">#![no_std]</span></code>.<sup about="#mwt623" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021213–215_96-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset2021213–215&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021213–215-96&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;213-215&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021213–215-96" id="mwCJ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJ8">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCKE">Rust uses the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Option_type" title="Option type" id="mwCKI">option type</a> <code id="mwCKM">Option&lt;T&gt;</code> to define optional values, which can be matched using <code id="mwCKQ">if let</code> or <code id="mwCKU">match</code> to access the inner value:<sup about="#mwt626" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023108–110,_113–114,_116–117_97-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023108–110, 113–114, 116–117&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023108–110,_113–114,_116–117-97&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;108-110,113-114,116-117&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023108–110,_113–114,_116–117-97" id="mwCKY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKg">[</span>92<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt629" id="mwCKo" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nfn main() {\n    let name1: Option<&amp;str> = None;\n    // In this case, nothing will be printed out\n    if let Some(name) = name1 {\n        println!(\&quot;{name}\&quot;);\n    }\n\n    let name2: Option<&amp;str> = Some(\&quot;Matthew\&quot;);\n    // In this case, the word \&quot;Matthew\&quot; will be printed out\n    if let Some(name) = name2 {\n        println!(\&quot;{name}\&quot;);\n    }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwCKs"><span id="mwCKw"></span><span class="k" id="mwCK0">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCK4"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCK8">main</span><span class="p" id="mwCLA">()</span><span class="w" id="mwCLE"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCLI">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCLM">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwCLQ">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCLU"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCLY">name1</span><span class="p" id="mwCLc">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCLg"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCLk">Option</span><span class="o" id="mwCLo">&lt;&amp;</span><span class="kt" id="mwCLs">str</span><span class="o" id="mwCLw">&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCL0"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCL4">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCL8"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCMA">None</span><span class="p" id="mwCME">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCMI">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwCMM">// In this case, nothing will be printed out</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCMQ">    </span><span class="k" id="mwCMU">if</span><span class="w" id="mwCMY"> </span><span class="kd" id="mwCMc">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCMg"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCMk">Some</span><span class="p" id="mwCMo">(</span><span class="n" id="mwCMs">name</span><span class="p" id="mwCMw">)</span><span class="w" id="mwCM0"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCM4">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCM8"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCNA">name1</span><span class="w" id="mwCNE"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCNI">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCNM">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwCNQ">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwCNU">(</span><span class="s" id="mwCNY">"{name}"</span><span class="p" id="mwCNc">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCNg">    </span><span class="p" id="mwCNk">}</span>

<span class="w" id="mwCNo">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwCNs">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCNw"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCN0">name2</span><span class="p" id="mwCN4">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCN8"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCOA">Option</span><span class="o" id="mwCOE">&lt;&amp;</span><span class="kt" id="mwCOI">str</span><span class="o" id="mwCOM">&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCOQ"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCOU">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCOY"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCOc">Some</span><span class="p" id="mwCOg">(</span><span class="s" id="mwCOk">"Matthew"</span><span class="p" id="mwCOo">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCOs">    </span><span class="c1" id="mwCOw">// In this case, the word "Matthew" will be printed out</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCO0">    </span><span class="k" id="mwCO4">if</span><span class="w" id="mwCO8"> </span><span class="kd" id="mwCPA">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCPE"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCPI">Some</span><span class="p" id="mwCPM">(</span><span class="n" id="mwCPQ">name</span><span class="p" id="mwCPU">)</span><span class="w" id="mwCPY"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCPc">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCPg"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCPk">name2</span><span class="w" id="mwCPo"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCPs">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCPw">        </span><span class="fm" id="mwCP0">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwCP4">(</span><span class="s" id="mwCP8">"{name}"</span><span class="p" id="mwCQA">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCQE">    </span><span class="p" id="mwCQI">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCQM">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwCQQ">Similarly, Rust's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Result_type" title="Result type" id="mwCQU">result type</a> <code id="mwCQY">Result&lt;T, E&gt;</code> holds either a successfully computed value (the <code id="mwCQc">Ok</code> variant) or an error (the <code id="mwCQg">Err</code> variant).<sup about="#mwt632" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rust_error_handling_98-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rust error handling&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rust_error_handling-98&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Rust_error_handling-98" id="mwCQk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQs">[</span>93<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQw">]</span></span></a></sup> Like <code id="mwCQ0">Option</code>, the use of <code id="mwCQ4">Result</code> means that the inner value cannot be used directly; programmers must use a <code id="mwCQ8">match</code> expression, syntactic sugar such as <code id="mwCRA">?</code> (the "try" operator), or an explicit <code id="mwCRE">unwrap</code> assertion to access it. Both <code id="mwCRI">Option</code> and <code id="mwCRM">Result</code> are used throughout the standard library and are a fundamental part of Rust's explicit approach to handling errors and missing data.</p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwCRQ" aria-labelledby="Pointers"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Pointers">Pointers</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23" title="Edit section: Pointers"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCRU">The <code id="mwCRY">&amp;</code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt633" id="mwCRc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&amp;mut&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;&amp;mut&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwCRg">&amp;</span><span class="k" id="mwCRk">mut</span></code> reference types are guaranteed to not be null and point to valid memory.<sup about="#mwt635" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021155-156_99-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset2021155-156&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021155-156-99&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;155-156&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021155-156-99" id="mwCRo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRw">[</span>94<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCR0">]</span></span></a></sup> The raw pointer types <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt638" id="mwCR4" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;*const&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;*const&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwCR8">*</span><span class="k" id="mwCSA">const</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt640" id="mwCSE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;*mut&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;*mut&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwCSI">*</span><span class="k" id="mwCSM">mut</span></code> opt out of the safety guarantees, thus they may be null or invalid; however, it is impossible to dereference them unless the code is explicitly declared unsafe through the use of an <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt642" id="mwCSQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCSU">unsafe</span></code> block.<sup about="#mwt644" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023421–423_100-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023421–423&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023421–423-100&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;421-423&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023421–423-100" id="mwCSY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSg">[</span>95<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSk">]</span></span></a></sup> Unlike dereferencing, the creation of raw pointers is allowed inside safe Rust code.<sup about="#mwt647" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019418–427_101-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019418–427&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019418–427-101&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;418–427&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019418–427-101" id="mwCSo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSw">[</span>96<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCS0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="24" id="mwCS4" aria-labelledby="Type_conversion"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Type_conversion">Type conversion</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24" title="Edit section: Type conversion"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt650" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCS8" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;excerpt&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Excerpt&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Type conversion&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rust&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt652" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">This section is an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_conversion#Rust" title="Type conversion">Type conversion § Rust</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Type_conversion&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Type_conversion&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p>Rust provides no implicit type conversion (coercion) between most primitive types. But, explicit type conversion (casting) can be performed using the <code>as</code> keyword.<sup about="#mwt655" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-102" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-102&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-102" id="mwCTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTI">[</span>97<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt658" id="mwCTQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nlet x: i32 = 1000;\nprintln!(\&quot;1000 as a u16 is: {}\&quot;, x as u16);\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwCTU"><span id="mwCTY"></span><span class="kd" id="mwCTc">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCTg"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCTk">x</span><span class="p" id="mwCTo">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCTs"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCTw">i32</span><span class="w" id="mwCT0"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCT4">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCT8"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwCUA">1000</span><span class="p" id="mwCUE">;</span>
<span class="fm" id="mwCUI">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwCUM">(</span><span class="s" id="mwCUQ">"1000 as a u16 is: {}"</span><span class="p" id="mwCUU">,</span><span class="w" id="mwCUY"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCUc">x</span><span class="w" id="mwCUg"> </span><span class="k" id="mwCUk">as</span><span class="w" id="mwCUo"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCUs">u16</span><span class="p" id="mwCUw">);</span>
</pre></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts"></span>
</div></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCU0"><span id="mwCU4"><video poster="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Rust_101.webm/250px--Rust_101.webm.jpg" controls="" preload="none" data-mw-tmh="" height="141" width="250" resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rust_101.webm" data-durationhint="5448" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCU8"><source src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/Rust_101.webm" type="video/webm; codecs=&quot;vp9, opus&quot;" data-file-width="1280" data-file-height="720" id="mwCVA"><source src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/Rust_101.webm/Rust_101.webm.240p.vp9.webm" type="video/webm; codecs=&quot;vp9, opus&quot;" data-width="426" data-height="240" data-transcodekey="240p.vp9.webm" id="mwCVE"><source src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/Rust_101.webm/Rust_101.webm.480p.vp9.webm" type="video/webm; codecs=&quot;vp9, opus&quot;" data-width="854" data-height="480" data-transcodekey="480p.vp9.webm" id="mwCVI"></video></span><figcaption id="mwCVM">A presentation on Rust by Emily Dunham from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla" title="Mozilla" id="mwCVQ">Mozilla</a>'s Rust team (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux.conf.au" title="Linux.conf.au" id="mwCVU">linux.conf.au</a> conference, Hobart, 2017)</figcaption></figure>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="25" id="mwCVY" aria-labelledby="Polymorphism"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Polymorphism">Polymorphism</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=25" title="Edit section: Polymorphism"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCVc">Rust supports <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polymorphism_(computer_science)" title="Polymorphism (computer science)" id="mwCVg">polymorphism</a> through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trait_(computer_programming)" title="Trait (computer programming)" id="mwCVk">traits</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generic_function" title="Generic function" id="mwCVo">generic functions</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trait_object_(Rust)" title="Trait object (Rust)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCVs">trait objects</a>.<sup about="#mwt659" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023378_103-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023378&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023378-103&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;378&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023378-103" id="mwCVw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCV0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCV4">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCV8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="26" id="mwCWA" aria-labelledby="Traits"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Traits">Traits</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=26" title="Edit section: Traits"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCWE">Common behavior between types is declared using traits and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt662" id="mwCWI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;impl&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;impl&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCWM">impl</span></code> blocks:<sup about="#mwt664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198_104-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198-104&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;192-198&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198-104" id="mwCWQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCWU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWY">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt667" id="mwCWg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\ntrait Zero: Sized {\n    fn zero() -> Self;\n    fn is_zero(&amp;self) -> bool\n    where\n        Self: PartialEq,\n    {\n        self == &amp;Zero::zero()\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Zero for u32 {\n    fn zero() -> u32 { 0 }\n}\n\nimpl Zero for f32 {\n    fn zero() -> Self { 0.0 }\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwCWk"><span id="mwCWo"></span><span class="k" id="mwCWs">trait</span><span class="w" id="mwCWw"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCW0">Zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCW4">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCW8"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCXA">Sized</span><span class="w" id="mwCXE"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCXI">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCXM">    </span><span class="k" id="mwCXQ">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCXU"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCXY">zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCXc">()</span><span class="w" id="mwCXg"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCXk">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCXo"> </span><span class="nc" id="mwCXs">Self</span><span class="p" id="mwCXw">;</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCX0">    </span><span class="k" id="mwCX4">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCX8"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCYA">is_zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCYE">(</span><span class="o" id="mwCYI">&amp;</span><span class="bp" id="mwCYM">self</span><span class="p" id="mwCYQ">)</span><span class="w" id="mwCYU"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCYY">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCYc"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCYg">bool</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCYk">    </span><span class="nc" id="mwCYo">where</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCYs">        </span><span class="bp" id="mwCYw">Self</span><span class="p" id="mwCY0">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCY4"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCY8">PartialEq</span><span class="p" id="mwCZA">,</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCZE">    </span><span class="p" id="mwCZI">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCZM">        </span><span class="bp" id="mwCZQ">self</span><span class="w" id="mwCZU"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCZY">==</span><span class="w" id="mwCZc"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCZg">&amp;</span><span class="n" id="mwCZk">Zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCZo">::</span><span class="n" id="mwCZs">zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCZw">()</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCZ0">    </span><span class="p" id="mwCZ4">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCZ8">}</span>

<span class="k" id="mwCaA">impl</span><span class="w" id="mwCaE"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCaI">Zero</span><span class="w" id="mwCaM"> </span><span class="k" id="mwCaQ">for</span><span class="w" id="mwCaU"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCaY">u32</span><span class="w" id="mwCac"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCag">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCak">    </span><span class="k" id="mwCao">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCas"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCaw">zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCa0">()</span><span class="w" id="mwCa4"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCa8">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCbA"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCbE">u32</span><span class="w" id="mwCbI"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCbM">{</span><span class="w" id="mwCbQ"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwCbU">0</span><span class="w" id="mwCbY"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCbc">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCbg">}</span>

<span class="k" id="mwCbk">impl</span><span class="w" id="mwCbo"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCbs">Zero</span><span class="w" id="mwCbw"> </span><span class="k" id="mwCb0">for</span><span class="w" id="mwCb4"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCb8">f32</span><span class="w" id="mwCcA"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCcE">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCcI">    </span><span class="k" id="mwCcM">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCcQ"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCcU">zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCcY">()</span><span class="w" id="mwCcc"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCcg">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCck"> </span><span class="nc" id="mwCco">Self</span><span class="w" id="mwCcs"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCcw">{</span><span class="w" id="mwCc0"> </span><span class="mf" id="mwCc4">0.0</span><span class="w" id="mwCc8"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCdA">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCdE">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwCdI">The example above includes a method <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt668" id="mwCdM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;is_zero&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;is_zero&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCdQ">is_zero</span></code> which provides a default implementation that may be overridden when implementing the trait.<sup about="#mwt670" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198_104-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198-104&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;192-198&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198-104" id="mwCdU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdc">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="27" id="mwCdk" aria-labelledby="Generic_functions"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Generic_functions">Generic functions</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=27" title="Edit section: Generic functions"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCdo">A function can be made generic by adding type parameters inside angle brackets (<code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt673" id="mwCds" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;<Num>&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;<Num>&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="o" id="mwCdw">&lt;</span><span class="n" id="mwCd0">Num</span><span class="o" id="mwCd4">&gt;</span></code>), which only allow types that implement the trait:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt675" id="mwCd8" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\n// zero is a generic function with one type parameter, Num\nfn zero<Num: Zero>() -> Num {\n    Num::zero()\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let a: u32 = zero();\n    let b: f32 = zero();\n    assert!(a.is_zero() &amp;&amp; b.is_zero());\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwCeA"><span id="mwCeE"></span><span class="c1" id="mwCeI">// zero is a generic function with one type parameter, Num</span>
<span class="k" id="mwCeM">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCeQ"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCeU">zero</span><span class="o" id="mwCeY">&lt;</span><span class="n" id="mwCec">Num</span><span class="p" id="mwCeg">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCek"> </span><span class="nc" id="mwCeo">Zero</span><span class="o" id="mwCes">&gt;</span><span class="p" id="mwCew">()</span><span class="w" id="mwCe0"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCe4">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCe8"> </span><span class="nc" id="mwCfA">Num</span><span class="w" id="mwCfE"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCfI">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCfM">    </span><span class="n" id="mwCfQ">Num</span><span class="p" id="mwCfU">::</span><span class="n" id="mwCfY">zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCfc">()</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCfg">}</span>

<span class="k" id="mwCfk">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwCfo"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwCfs">main</span><span class="p" id="mwCfw">()</span><span class="w" id="mwCf0"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCf4">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCf8">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwCgA">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCgE"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCgI">a</span><span class="p" id="mwCgM">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCgQ"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwCgU">u32</span><span class="w" id="mwCgY"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCgc">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCgg"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCgk">zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCgo">();</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCgs">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwCgw">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCg0"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCg4">b</span><span class="p" id="mwCg8">:</span><span class="w" id="mwChA"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwChE">f32</span><span class="w" id="mwChI"> </span><span class="o" id="mwChM">=</span><span class="w" id="mwChQ"> </span><span class="n" id="mwChU">zero</span><span class="p" id="mwChY">();</span>
<span class="w" id="mwChc">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwChg">assert!</span><span class="p" id="mwChk">(</span><span class="n" id="mwCho">a</span><span class="p" id="mwChs">.</span><span class="n" id="mwChw">is_zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCh0">()</span><span class="w" id="mwCh4"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCh8">&amp;&amp;</span><span class="w" id="mwCiA"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCiE">b</span><span class="p" id="mwCiI">.</span><span class="n" id="mwCiM">is_zero</span><span class="p" id="mwCiQ">());</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCiU">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwCiY">In the examples above, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt676" id="mwCic" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Num: Zero&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Num: Zero&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCig">Num</span><span class="p" id="mwCik">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCio"> </span><span class="nc" id="mwCis">Zero</span></code> as well as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt678" id="mwCiw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;where Self: PartialEq&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;where Self: PartialEq&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCi0">where</span><span class="w" id="mwCi4"> </span><span class="bp" id="mwCi8">Self</span><span class="p" id="mwCjA">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCjE"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCjI">PartialEq</span></code> are trait bounds that constrain the type to only allow types that implement <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt680" id="mwCjM" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Zero&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Zero&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwCjQ">Zero</span></code> or <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt682" id="mwCjU" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;PartialEq&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;PartialEq&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="nb" id="mwCjY">PartialEq</span></code>.<sup about="#mwt684" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198_104-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198-104&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;192-198&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023192–198-104" id="mwCjc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjk">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjo">]</span></span></a></sup> Within a trait or impl, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt687" id="mwCjs" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Self&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Self&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="bp" id="mwCjw">Self</span></code> refers to the type that the code is implementing.<sup about="#mwt689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202398_105-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202398&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202398-105&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;98&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols202398-105" id="mwCj0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCj4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCj8">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCkE">Generics can be used in functions to allow implementing a behavior for different types without repeating the same code (see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bounded_parametric_polymorphism" title="Bounded parametric polymorphism" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCkI">bounded parametric polymorphism</a>). Generic functions can be written in relation to other generics, without knowing the actual type.<sup about="#mwt692" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019171–172,_205_106-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019171–172, 205&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019171–172,_205-106&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;171–172,205&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019171–172,_205-106" id="mwCkM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCkQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkU">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="28" id="mwCkc" aria-labelledby="Trait_objects"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Trait_objects">Trait objects</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=28" title="Edit section: Trait objects"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCkg">By default, traits use <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Static_dispatch" title="Static dispatch" id="mwCkk">static dispatch</a>: the compiler <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monomorphization" title="Monomorphization" id="mwCko">monomorphizes</a> the function for each concrete type instance, yielding performance equivalent to type-specific code at the cost of longer compile times and larger binaries.<sup about="#mwt695" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192_107-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192-107&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;191-192&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192-107" id="mwCks"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCkw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCk0">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCk4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCk8">When the exact type is not known at compile time, Rust provides <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trait_object_(Rust)" title="Trait object (Rust)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwClA">trait objects</a> <code id="mwClE">&amp;dyn Trait</code> and <code id="mwClI">Box&lt;dyn Trait&gt;</code>.<sup about="#mwt698" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019441–442_108-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019441–442&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019441–442-108&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;441–442&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019441–442-108" id="mwClM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClU">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClY">]</span></span></a></sup> Trait object calls use <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_dispatch" title="Dynamic dispatch" id="mwClc">dynamic dispatch</a> via a lookup table; a trait object is a "fat pointer" carrying both a data pointer and a method table pointer.<sup about="#mwt701" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192_107-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192-107&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;191-192&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023191–192-107" id="mwClg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClo">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCls">]</span></span></a></sup> This indirection adds a small runtime cost, but it keeps a single copy of the code and reduces binary size. Only "object-safe" traits are eligible to be used as trait objects.<sup about="#mwt704" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset202125_109-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset202125&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset202125-109&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;25&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset202125-109" id="mwClw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCl0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCl4">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCl8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCmA">This approach is similar to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck_typing" title="Duck typing" id="mwCmE">duck typing</a>, where all data types that implement a given trait can be treated as functionally interchangeable.<sup about="#mwt707" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch18-02-trait-objectshtml_18.2._Using_Trait_Objects_That_Allow_for_Values_of_Different_Types]_110-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch18-02-trait-objectshtml 18.2. Using Trait Objects That Allow for Values of Different Types]&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch18-02-trait-objectshtml_18.2._Using_Trait_Objects_That_Allow_for_Values_of_Different_Types]-110&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;loc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch18-02-trait-objects.html 18.2. Using Trait Objects That Allow for Values of Different Types]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023[httpsdocrust-langorgbookch18-02-trait-objectshtml_18.2._Using_Trait_Objects_That_Allow_for_Values_of_Different_Types]-110" id="mwCmI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCmM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmQ">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmU">]</span></span></a></sup> The following example creates a list of objects where each object implements the <code id="mwCmY">Display</code> trait:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt710" id="mwCmc" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;Rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\nuse std::fmt::Display;\n\nlet v: Vec<Box<dyn Display>> = vec![\n    Box::new(3),\n    Box::new(5.0),\n    Box::new(\&quot;hi\&quot;),\n];\n\nfor x in v {\n    println!(\&quot;{x}\&quot;);\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwCmg"><span id="mwCmk"></span><span class="k" id="mwCmo">use</span><span class="w" id="mwCms"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCmw">std</span><span class="p" id="mwCm0">::</span><span class="n" id="mwCm4">fmt</span><span class="p" id="mwCm8">::</span><span class="n" id="mwCnA">Display</span><span class="p" id="mwCnE">;</span>

<span class="kd" id="mwCnI">let</span><span class="w" id="mwCnM"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCnQ">v</span><span class="p" id="mwCnU">:</span><span class="w" id="mwCnY"> </span><span class="nb" id="mwCnc">Vec</span><span class="o" id="mwCng">&lt;</span><span class="nb" id="mwCnk">Box</span><span class="o" id="mwCno">&lt;</span><span class="k" id="mwCns">dyn</span><span class="w" id="mwCnw"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCn0">Display</span><span class="o" id="mwCn4">&gt;&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCn8"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCoA">=</span><span class="w" id="mwCoE"> </span><span class="fm" id="mwCoI">vec!</span><span class="p" id="mwCoM">[</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCoQ">    </span><span class="nb" id="mwCoU">Box</span><span class="p" id="mwCoY">::</span><span class="n" id="mwCoc">new</span><span class="p" id="mwCog">(</span><span class="mi" id="mwCok">3</span><span class="p" id="mwCoo">),</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCos">    </span><span class="nb" id="mwCow">Box</span><span class="p" id="mwCo0">::</span><span class="n" id="mwCo4">new</span><span class="p" id="mwCo8">(</span><span class="mf" id="mwCpA">5.0</span><span class="p" id="mwCpE">),</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCpI">    </span><span class="nb" id="mwCpM">Box</span><span class="p" id="mwCpQ">::</span><span class="n" id="mwCpU">new</span><span class="p" id="mwCpY">(</span><span class="s" id="mwCpc">"hi"</span><span class="p" id="mwCpg">),</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCpk">];</span>

<span class="k" id="mwCpo">for</span><span class="w" id="mwCps"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCpw">x</span><span class="w" id="mwCp0"> </span><span class="k" id="mwCp4">in</span><span class="w" id="mwCp8"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCqA">v</span><span class="w" id="mwCqE"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCqI">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCqM">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwCqQ">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwCqU">(</span><span class="s" id="mwCqY">"{x}"</span><span class="p" id="mwCqc">);</span>
<span class="p" id="mwCqg">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwCqk">If an element in the list does not implement the <code id="mwCqo">Display</code> trait, it will cause a compile-time error.<sup about="#mwt711" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019379–380_111-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019379–380&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019379–380-111&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;379–380&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019379–380-111" id="mwCqs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCqw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCq0">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCq4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="29" id="mwCq8" aria-labelledby="Memory_management"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Memory_management">Memory management</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=29" title="Edit section: Memory management"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCrA">Rust does not use <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garbage_collection_(computer_science)" title="Garbage collection (computer science)" id="mwCrE">garbage collection</a>. Memory and other resources are instead managed through the "resource acquisition is initialization" convention,<sup about="#mwt716" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-112" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-112&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-112" id="mwCrI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCrM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrQ">[</span>107<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrU">]</span></span></a></sup> with optional <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reference_counting" title="Reference counting" id="mwCrY">reference counting</a>. Rust provides deterministic management of resources, with very low <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Overhead_(computing)" title="Overhead (computing)" id="mwCrc">overhead</a>.<sup about="#mwt719" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-113" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-113&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-113" id="mwCrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCrk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCro">[</span>108<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrs">]</span></span></a></sup> Values are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stack-based_memory_allocation" title="Stack-based memory allocation" id="mwCrw">allocated on the stack</a> by default, and all <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_allocation" title="Dynamic allocation" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCr0">dynamic allocations</a> must be explicit.<sup about="#mwt722" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-114" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-114&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-114" id="mwCr4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCr8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsA">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCsI">The built-in reference types using the <code id="mwCsM">&amp;</code> symbol do not involve run-time reference counting. The safety and validity of the underlying pointers are verified at compile time, preventing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dangling_pointers" title="Dangling pointers" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCsQ">dangling pointers</a> and other forms of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Undefined_behavior" title="Undefined behavior" id="mwCsU">undefined behavior</a>.<sup about="#mwt723" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201970–75_115-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201970–75&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201970–75-115&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;70–75&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols201970–75-115" id="mwCsY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCsc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsg">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsk">]</span></span></a></sup> Rust's type system separates shared, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Immutable" title="Immutable" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCso">immutable</a> references of the form <code id="mwCss">&amp;T</code> from unique, mutable references of the form <code id="mwCsw">&amp;mut T</code>. A mutable reference can be coerced to an immutable reference, but not vice versa.<sup about="#mwt726" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019323_116-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019323&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019323-116&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;323&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019323-116" id="mwCs0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCs4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCs8">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="30" id="mwCtE" aria-labelledby="Unsafe"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Unsafe">Unsafe</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=30" title="Edit section: Unsafe"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCtI">Rust's memory safety checks (See <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Safety" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwCtM">#Safety</a>) may be circumvented through the use of <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt729" id="mwCtQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwCtU">unsafe</span></code> blocks. This allows programmers to dereference arbitrary raw pointers, call external code, or perform other low-level functionality not allowed by safe Rust.<sup about="#mwt731" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023420–429_117-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023420–429&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023420–429-117&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;420-429&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023420–429-117" id="mwCtY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCtc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtg">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtk">]</span></span></a></sup> Some low-level functionality enabled in this way includes <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volatile_(computer_programming)" title="Volatile (computer programming)" id="mwCto">volatile memory access</a>, architecture-specific intrinsics, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_punning" title="Type punning" id="mwCts">type punning</a>, and inline assembly.<sup about="#mwt734" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcNamara2021139,_376–379,_395_118-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMcNamara2021139, 376–379, 395&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara2021139,_376–379,_395-118&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;McNamara&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;139, 376–379, 395&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara2021139,_376–379,_395-118" id="mwCtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCt0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCt4">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCt8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCuA">Unsafe code is needed, for example, in the implementation of data structures.<sup about="#mwt739" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-UnsafeRustUse_119-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;UnsafeRustUse&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-UnsafeRustUse-119&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-UnsafeRustUse-119" id="mwCuE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuM">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuQ">]</span></span></a></sup> A frequently cited example is that it is difficult or impossible to implement <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doubly_linked_list" title="Doubly linked list" id="mwCuU">doubly linked lists</a> in safe Rust.<sup about="#mwt742" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-120" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-120&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-120" id="mwCuY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCug">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt745" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-121" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-121&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-121" id="mwCuo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCus"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuw">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCu0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt748" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-122" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-122&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-122" id="mwCu4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCu8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvA">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt751" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-123&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwCvI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCvM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvQ">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCvY">Programmers using unsafe Rust are considered responsible for upholding Rust's memory and type safety requirements, for example, that no two mutable references exist pointing to the same location.<sup about="#mwt754" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IsRustSafely_124-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;IsRustSafely&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-IsRustSafely-124&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-IsRustSafely-124" id="mwCvc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvk">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvo">]</span></span></a></sup> If programmers write code that violates these requirements, this results in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Undefined_behavior" title="Undefined behavior" id="mwCvs">undefined behavior</a>.<sup about="#mwt755" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IsRustSafely_124-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;IsRustSafely&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-IsRustSafely-124" id="mwCvw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCv0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCv4">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCv8">]</span></span></a></sup> The Rust documentation includes a list of behaviors considered undefined, including accessing dangling or misaligned pointers, or breaking the aliasing rules for references.<sup about="#mwt758" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-125" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-125&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-125" id="mwCwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwI">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<!--
=== Closures ===
-->

</section><section data-mw-section-id="31" id="mwCwQ" aria-labelledby="Macros"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Macros">Macros</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=31" title="Edit section: Macros"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCwU">Macros allow the generation and transformation of Rust code to reduce repetition. Macros come in two forms, with <i id="mwCwY">declarative macros</i> defined through <code id="mwCwc">macro_rules!</code>, and <i id="mwCwg">procedural macros</i>, which are defined in separate crates.<sup about="#mwt759" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023449–455_126-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023449–455&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023449–455-126&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;449–455&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023449–455-126" id="mwCwk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCws">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCww">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt762" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021101–102_127-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset2021101–102&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021101–102-127&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;101-102&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021101–102-127" id="mwCw0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCw4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCw8">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="32" id="mwCxE" aria-labelledby="Declarative_macros"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Declarative_macros">Declarative macros</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=32" title="Edit section: Declarative macros"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwCxI">A declarative macro (also called a "macro by example") is a macro, defined using the <code id="mwCxM">macro_rules!</code> keyword, that uses pattern matching to determine its expansion.<sup about="#mwt770" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rust_Ref._–_Macros_By_Example_128-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rust Ref. – Macros By Example&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rust_Ref._–_Macros_By_Example-128&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Rust_Ref._–_Macros_By_Example-128" id="mwCxQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxY">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019446–448_129-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019446–448&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019446–448-129&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;446–448&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019446–448-129" id="mwCxg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxo">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxs">]</span></span></a></sup> Below is an example that sums over all its arguments:</p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt771" id="mwCxw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;macro_rules! sum {\n    ( $initial:expr $(, $expr:expr )* $(,)? ) => {\n        $initial $(+ $expr)*\n    }\n}\n\nfn main() {\n    let x = sum!(1, 2, 3);\n    println!(\&quot;{x}\&quot;); // prints 6\n}&quot;}}"><pre id="mwCx0"><span id="mwCx4"></span><span class="fm" id="mwCx8">macro_rules!</span><span class="w" id="mwCyA"> </span><span class="n" id="mwCyE">sum</span><span class="w" id="mwCyI"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCyM">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCyQ">    </span><span class="p" id="mwCyU">(</span><span class="w" id="mwCyY"> </span><span class="cp" id="mwCyc">$initial</span><span class="p" id="mwCyg">:</span><span class="nc" id="mwCyk">expr</span><span class="w" id="mwCyo"> </span><span class="cp" id="mwCys">$(,</span><span class="w" id="mwCyw"> </span><span class="cp" id="mwCy0">$expr</span><span class="p" id="mwCy4">:</span><span class="nc" id="mwCy8">expr</span><span class="w" id="mwCzA"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCzE">)</span><span class="o" id="mwCzI">*</span><span class="w" id="mwCzM"> </span><span class="cp" id="mwCzQ">$(,</span><span class="p" id="mwCzU">)</span><span class="o" id="mwCzY">?</span><span class="w" id="mwCzc"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCzg">)</span><span class="w" id="mwCzk"> </span><span class="o" id="mwCzo">=&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwCzs"> </span><span class="p" id="mwCzw">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwCz0">        </span><span class="cp" id="mwCz4">$initial</span><span class="w" id="mwCz8"> </span><span class="cp" id="mwC0A">$(</span><span class="o" id="mwC0E">+</span><span class="w" id="mwC0I"> </span><span class="cp" id="mwC0M">$expr</span><span class="p" id="mwC0Q">)</span><span class="o" id="mwC0U">*</span>
<span class="w" id="mwC0Y">    </span><span class="p" id="mwC0c">}</span>
<span class="p" id="mwC0g">}</span>

<span class="k" id="mwC0k">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwC0o"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwC0s">main</span><span class="p" id="mwC0w">()</span><span class="w" id="mwC00"> </span><span class="p" id="mwC04">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwC08">    </span><span class="kd" id="mwC1A">let</span><span class="w" id="mwC1E"> </span><span class="n" id="mwC1I">x</span><span class="w" id="mwC1M"> </span><span class="o" id="mwC1Q">=</span><span class="w" id="mwC1U"> </span><span class="n" id="mwC1Y">sum</span><span class="o" id="mwC1c">!</span><span class="p" id="mwC1g">(</span><span class="mi" id="mwC1k">1</span><span class="p" id="mwC1o">,</span><span class="w" id="mwC1s"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwC1w">2</span><span class="p" id="mwC10">,</span><span class="w" id="mwC14"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwC18">3</span><span class="p" id="mwC2A">);</span>
<span class="w" id="mwC2E">    </span><span class="fm" id="mwC2I">println!</span><span class="p" id="mwC2M">(</span><span class="s" id="mwC2Q">"{x}"</span><span class="p" id="mwC2U">);</span><span class="w" id="mwC2Y"> </span><span class="c1" id="mwC2c">// prints 6</span>
<span class="p" id="mwC2g">}</span>
</pre></div>
<p id="mwC2k">In this example, the macro named <code id="mwC2o">sum</code> is defined using the form <code id="mwC2s">macro_rules! sum {</code> <code id="mwC2w">(...) =&gt; { ... } }</code>. The first part inside the parentheses of the definition, the macro pattern <code id="mwC20">( $initial:expr $(, $expr:expr )* $(,)? )</code> specifies the structure of input it can take. Here, <code id="mwC24">$initial:expr</code> represents the first expression, while <code id="mwC28">$(, $expr:expr )*</code> means there can be zero or more additional comma-separated expressions after it. The trailing <code id="mwC3A">$(,)?</code> allows the caller to optionally include a final comma without causing an error. The second part, after the arrow <code id="mwC3E">=&gt;</code>, describes what code will be generated when the macro is invoked. In this case, <code id="mwC3I">$initial $(+ $expr)*</code> means that the generated code will start with the first expression, followed by a <code id="mwC3M">+</code> and each of the additional expressions in sequence. The <code id="mwC3Q">*</code> again means "repeat this pattern zero or more times". This means, when the macro is later called in line 8, as <code id="mwC3U">sum!(1, 2, 3)</code>, the macro will resolve to <code id="mwC3Y">1 + 2 + 3</code> representing the addition of all of the passed expressions.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="33" id="mwC3c" aria-labelledby="Procedural_macros"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Procedural_macros">Procedural macros</h4><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=33" title="Edit section: Procedural macros"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwC3g">Procedural macros are Rust functions that run and modify the compiler's input <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Token_(parser)" title="Token (parser)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC3k">token</a> stream, before any other components are compiled. They are generally more flexible than declarative macros, but are more difficult to maintain due to their complexity.<sup about="#mwt777" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rust-procedural-macros_130-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;rust-procedural-macros&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-rust-procedural-macros-130&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-rust-procedural-macros-130" id="mwC3o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3w">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC30">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt772" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019449–455_131-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019449–455&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019449–455-131&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;449–455&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019449–455-131" id="mwC34"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC38"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4A">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC4I">Procedural macros come in three flavors:</p>
<ul id="mwC4M"><li id="mwC4Q">Function-like macros <code id="mwC4U">custom!(...)</code></li>
<li id="mwC4Y">Derive macros <code id="mwC4c">#[derive(CustomDerive)]</code></li>
<li id="mwC4g">Attribute macros <code id="mwC4k">#[custom_attribute]</code></li></ul>
<!-- TODO example -->

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="34" id="mwC4o" aria-labelledby="Interface_with_C_and_C++"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Interface_with_C_and_C++"><span id="Interface_with_C_and_C.2B.2B" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Interface with C and C++</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=34" title="Edit section: Interface with C and C++"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwC4s">Rust supports the creation of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_function_interface" title="Foreign function interface" id="mwC4w">foreign function interfaces</a> (FFI) through the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt778" id="mwC40" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;extern&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;extern&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwC44">extern</span></code> keyword. A function that uses the C <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calling_convention" title="Calling convention" id="mwC48">calling convention</a> can be written using <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt780" id="mwC5A" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;extern \&quot;C\&quot; fn&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;extern \&quot;C\&quot; fn&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwC5E">extern</span><span class="w" id="mwC5I"> </span><span class="s" id="mwC5M">"C"</span><span class="w" id="mwC5Q"> </span><span class="k" id="mwC5U">fn</span></code>. Symbols can be exported from Rust to other languages through the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt782" id="mwC5Y" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;#[unsafe(no_mangle)]&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#[unsafe(no_mangle)]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="cp" id="mwC5c">#[unsafe(no_mangle)]</span></code> attribute, and symbols can be imported into Rust through <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt784" id="mwC5g" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;extern&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;extern&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwC5k">extern</span></code> blocks:<sup about="#mwt786" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-133" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-133&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;refn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Refn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;wrapping {{code|no_mangle}} with {{rust|unsafe}} as well as prefacing the {{rust|extern \&quot;C\&quot;}} block with {{rust|unsafe}} are required in the 2024 edition or later.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Baumgartner |first=Stefan |date=2025-05-23 |title=Programming language: Rust 2024 is the most comprehensive edition to date |url=https://www.heise.de/en/background/Programming-language-Rust-2024-is-the-most-comprehensive-edition-to-date-10393917.html |access-date=2025-06-28 |website=[[heise online]] |language=en}}</ref>&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-133" data-mw-group="note" id="mwC5o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC5s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC5w">[</span>note 6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC50">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt804" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209_134-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209-134&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;193-209&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209-134" id="mwC54"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC58"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6A">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt807" id="mwC6I" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;\n#[unsafe(no_mangle)]\npub extern \&quot;C\&quot; fn exported_from_rust(x: i32) -> i32 { x + 1 }\nunsafe extern \&quot;C\&quot; {\n    fn imported_into_rust(x: i32) -> i32;\n}\n&quot;}}"><pre id="mwC6M"><span id="mwC6Q"></span><span class="cp" id="mwC6U">#[unsafe(no_mangle)]</span>
<span class="k" id="mwC6Y">pub</span><span class="w" id="mwC6c"> </span><span class="k" id="mwC6g">extern</span><span class="w" id="mwC6k"> </span><span class="s" id="mwC6o">"C"</span><span class="w" id="mwC6s"> </span><span class="k" id="mwC6w">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwC60"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwC64">exported_from_rust</span><span class="p" id="mwC68">(</span><span class="n" id="mwC7A">x</span><span class="p" id="mwC7E">:</span><span class="w" id="mwC7I"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwC7M">i32</span><span class="p" id="mwC7Q">)</span><span class="w" id="mwC7U"> </span><span class="p" id="mwC7Y">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwC7c"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwC7g">i32</span><span class="w" id="mwC7k"> </span><span class="p" id="mwC7o">{</span><span class="w" id="mwC7s"> </span><span class="n" id="mwC7w">x</span><span class="w" id="mwC70"> </span><span class="o" id="mwC74">+</span><span class="w" id="mwC78"> </span><span class="mi" id="mwC8A">1</span><span class="w" id="mwC8E"> </span><span class="p" id="mwC8I">}</span>
<span class="k" id="mwC8M">unsafe</span><span class="w" id="mwC8Q"> </span><span class="k" id="mwC8U">extern</span><span class="w" id="mwC8Y"> </span><span class="s" id="mwC8c">"C"</span><span class="w" id="mwC8g"> </span><span class="p" id="mwC8k">{</span>
<span class="w" id="mwC8o">    </span><span class="k" id="mwC8s">fn</span><span class="w" id="mwC8w"> </span><span class="nf" id="mwC80">imported_into_rust</span><span class="p" id="mwC84">(</span><span class="n" id="mwC88">x</span><span class="p" id="mwC9A">:</span><span class="w" id="mwC9E"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwC9I">i32</span><span class="p" id="mwC9M">)</span><span class="w" id="mwC9Q"> </span><span class="p" id="mwC9U">-&gt;</span><span class="w" id="mwC9Y"> </span><span class="kt" id="mwC9c">i32</span><span class="p" id="mwC9g">;</span>
<span class="p" id="mwC9k">}</span>
</pre></div>

<p id="mwC9o">The <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt808" id="mwC9s" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;#[repr(C)]&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;#[repr(C)]&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="cp" id="mwC9w">#[repr(C)]</span></code> attribute enables deterministic memory layouts for <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt810" id="mwC90" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;struct&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;struct&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwC94">struct</span></code>s and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt812" id="mwC98" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;enum&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;enum&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwC-A">enum</span></code>s for use across FFI boundaries.<sup about="#mwt814" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209_134-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209-134&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;193-209&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209-134" id="mwC-E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-M">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-Q">]</span></span></a></sup> External libraries such as <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt817" id="mwC-U" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;bindgen&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;bindgen&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwC-Y">bindgen</span></code> and <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt819" id="mwC-c" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;cxx&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;cxx&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="n" id="mwC-g">cxx</span></code> can generate Rust bindings for C/C++.<sup about="#mwt821" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209_134-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209-134&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;193-209&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset2021193–209-134" id="mwC-k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-s">[</span>128<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt826" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-135" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-135&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-135" id="mwC-0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-8">[</span>129<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="35" id="mwC_E" aria-labelledby="Safety"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Safety">Safety</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=35" title="Edit section: Safety"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwC_I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Safety_properties" title="Safety properties" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC_M">Safety properties</a> guaranteed by Rust include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_safety" title="Memory safety" id="mwC_Q">memory safety</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Type_safety" title="Type safety" id="mwC_U">type safety</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_race" title="Data race" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC_Y">data race</a> freedom. As described above, these guarantees can be circumvented by using the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt827" id="mwC_c" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwC_g">unsafe</span></code> keyword.</p>

<p id="mwC_k">Memory safety includes the absence of dereferences to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Null_pointer" title="Null pointer" id="mwC_o">null</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dangling_pointer" title="Dangling pointer" id="mwC_s">dangling</a>, and misaligned <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pointer_(computer_programming)" title="Pointer (computer programming)" id="mwC_w">pointers</a>, and the absence of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buffer_overflow" title="Buffer overflow" id="mwC_0">buffer overflows</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Double_free" title="Double free" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC_4">double free</a> errors.<sup about="#mwt831" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-cnet_136-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;cnet&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-cnet-136&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-cnet-136" id="mwC_8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAE">[</span>130<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt834" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-lwn_137-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;lwn&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-lwn-137&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-lwn-137" id="mwDAM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAU">[</span>131<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt837" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-The_Rustonomicon_138-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;The Rustonomicon&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-The_Rustonomicon-138&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-The_Rustonomicon-138" id="mwDAc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAk">[</span>132<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt840" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Sensors_139-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Sensors&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Sensors-139&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Sensors-139" id="mwDAs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA0">[</span>133<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDA8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memory_leak" title="Memory leak" id="mwDBA">Memory leaks</a> are possible in safe Rust.<sup about="#mwt841" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346_140-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346-140&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;343-346&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346-140" id="mwDBE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDBI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBM">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Memory leaks may occur as a result of creating reference-counted pointers that point at each other (a reference cycle)<sup about="#mwt844" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346_140-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346-140&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;343-346&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023343–346-140" id="mwDBU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDBY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBc">[</span>134<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBg">]</span></span></a></sup> or can be deliberately created through calling <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt847" id="mwDBk" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;style&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;Box::leak&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;code&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Code&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Box::leak&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">Box::leak</code>.<sup about="#mwt849" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset20216_141-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset20216&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset20216-141&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;6&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset20216-141" id="mwDBo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDBs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBw">[</span>135<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDB0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="36" id="mwDB4" aria-labelledby="Ecosystem"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Ecosystem">Ecosystem</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=36" title="Edit section: Ecosystem"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDB8"><span id="mwDCA"><video poster="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Cargo_compiling.webm/250px--Cargo_compiling.webm.jpg" controls="" preload="none" data-mw-tmh="" height="140" width="250" resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cargo_compiling.webm" data-durationhint="20" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDCE"><source src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/Cargo_compiling.webm" type="video/webm; codecs=&quot;vp9&quot;" data-file-width="1508" data-file-height="844" id="mwDCI"><source src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/52/Cargo_compiling.webm/Cargo_compiling.webm.240p.vp9.webm" type="video/webm; codecs=&quot;vp9, opus&quot;" data-width="426" data-height="238" data-transcodekey="240p.vp9.webm" id="mwDCM"><source src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/52/Cargo_compiling.webm/Cargo_compiling.webm.480p.vp9.webm" type="video/webm; codecs=&quot;vp9, opus&quot;" data-width="854" data-height="478" data-transcodekey="480p.vp9.webm" id="mwDCQ"></video></span><figcaption id="mwDCU">Compiling a Rust program with Cargo</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwDCY">The Rust ecosystem includes its compiler, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Standard_library" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwDCc">its standard library</a>, and additional components for software development. Component installation is typically managed by <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt852" id="mwDCg" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;style&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;rustup&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;code&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Code&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rustup&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">rustup</code>, a Rust <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toolchain" title="Toolchain" id="mwDCk">toolchain</a> installer developed by the Rust project.<sup about="#mwt854" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall20216–8_142-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall20216–8&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall20216–8-142&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Blandy&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Orendorff&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tindall&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;6-8&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall20216–8-142" id="mwDCo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDCs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCw">[</span>136<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDC0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<!-- Add Miri Compiler? -->

<section data-mw-section-id="37" id="mwDC4" aria-labelledby="Compiler"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Compiler">Compiler</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=37" title="Edit section: Compiler"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDC8">The Rust compiler, <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt857" id="mwDDA" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;style&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;rustc&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;code&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Code&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rustc&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">rustc</code>, compiles Rust code into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executable" title="Executable" id="mwDDE">binaries</a>. First, the compiler parses the source code into an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abstract_syntax_tree" title="Abstract syntax tree" id="mwDDI">AST</a>. Next, this AST is lowered to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intermediate_representation" title="Intermediate representation" id="mwDDM">IR</a>. The compiler backend is then invoked as a subcomponent to apply <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optimizing_compiler" title="Optimizing compiler" id="mwDDQ">optimizations</a> and translate the resulting IR into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object_code" title="Object code" id="mwDDU">object code</a>. Finally, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linker_(computing)" title="Linker (computing)" id="mwDDY">linker</a> is used to combine the object(s) into a single executable image.<sup about="#mwt861" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-143" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-143&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-143" id="mwDDc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDDg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDk">[</span>137<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDDs">rustc uses <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LLVM" title="LLVM" id="mwDDw">LLVM</a> as its compiler backend by default, but it also supports using alternative backends such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Compiler_Collection" title="GNU Compiler Collection" id="mwDD0">GCC</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cranelift" title="Cranelift" id="mwDD4">Cranelift</a>.<sup about="#mwt864" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-144" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-144&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-144" id="mwDD8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEE">[</span>138<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEI">]</span></span></a></sup> The intention of those alternative backends is to increase platform coverage of Rust or to improve compilation times.<sup about="#mwt867" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-145" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-145&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-145" id="mwDEM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEU">[</span>139<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt870" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-146" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-146&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-146" id="mwDEc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEk">[</span>140<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="38" id="mwDEs" aria-labelledby="Cargo"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Cargo">Cargo</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=38" title="Edit section: Cargo"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDEw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Crates.io_website.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDE0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Crates.io_website.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Crates.io_website.png/250px-Crates.io_website.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="2102" data-file-height="1202" data-file-type="bitmap" height="143" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Crates.io_website.png/500px-Crates.io_website.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDE4"></a><figcaption id="mwDE8">Screenshot of crates.io in June 2022</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDFA">Cargo is Rust's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Build_system_(software_development)" title="Build system (software development)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDFE">build system</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Package_manager" title="Package manager" id="mwDFI">package manager</a>. It downloads, compiles, distributes, and uploads packages—called <i id="mwDFM">crates</i>—that are maintained in an official registry. It also acts as a front-end for Clippy and other Rust components.<sup about="#mwt873" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Nature_147-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Nature&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Nature-147&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Nature-147" id="mwDFQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDFU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFY">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDFg">By default, Cargo sources its dependencies from the user-contributed registry <i id="mwDFk">crates.io</i>, but <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Git" title="Git" id="mwDFo">Git</a> repositories, crates in the local filesystem, and other external sources can also be specified as dependencies.<sup about="#mwt876" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-148" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-148&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-148" id="mwDFs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDFw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDF0">[</span>142<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDF4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDF8">Cargo supports reproducible builds through two metadata files: Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock.<sup about="#mwt879" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-149" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-149&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-149" id="mwDGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGI">[</span>143<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGM">]</span></span></a></sup> Cargo.toml declares each package used and their version requirements. Cargo.lock is generated automatically during dependency resolution and records exact versions of all dependencies, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transitive_dependency" title="Transitive dependency" id="mwDGQ">transitive dependencies</a>.<sup about="#mwt882" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-150" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-150&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-150" id="mwDGU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGc">[</span>144<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="39" id="mwDGk" aria-labelledby="Rustfmt"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Rustfmt">Rustfmt</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=39" title="Edit section: Rustfmt"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDGo">Rustfmt is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_formatter" title="Code formatter" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDGs">code formatter</a> for Rust. It formats whitespace and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indentation_style" title="Indentation style" id="mwDGw">indentation</a> to produce code in accordance with a common <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programming_style" title="Programming style" id="mwDG0">style</a>, unless otherwise specified. It can be invoked as a standalone program or from a Rust project through Cargo.<sup about="#mwt883" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019511–512_151-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019511–512&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019511–512-151&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;511–512&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2019511–512-151" id="mwDG4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDG8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHA">[</span>145<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="40" id="mwDHI" aria-labelledby="Clippy"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Clippy">Clippy</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=40" title="Edit section: Clippy"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDHM"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cargo_clippy_hello_world_example.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDHQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Cargo_clippy_hello_world_example.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Cargo_clippy_hello_world_example.png/250px-Cargo_clippy_hello_world_example.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="912" data-file-height="704" data-file-type="bitmap" height="193" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Cargo_clippy_hello_world_example.png/500px-Cargo_clippy_hello_world_example.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDHU"></a><figcaption id="mwDHY">Example output of Clippy on a hello world Rust program</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDHc">Clippy is Rust's built-in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linting" title="Linting" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDHg">linting</a> tool to improve the correctness, performance, and readability of Rust code. <span about="#mwt886" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDHk" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;as of&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:As_of&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2026&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">As of 2026</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt886"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt886"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_2026" about="#mwt886"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt886" id="mwDHo">, it has over 800 rules.<sup about="#mwt889" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-152" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-152&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-152" id="mwDHs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDH0">[</span>146<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDH4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt892" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-153" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-153&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-153" id="mwDH8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIE">[</span>147<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDII">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="41" id="mwDIM" aria-labelledby="Versioning_system"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Versioning_system">Versioning system</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=41" title="Edit section: Versioning system"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDIQ">Following Rust 1.0, new features are developed in <i id="mwDIU">nightly</i> versions, which are released daily. During each six-week release cycle, changes to nightly versions are released to beta, while changes from the previous beta version are released to a new stable version.<sup about="#mwt894" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Rust_Book_G_154-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Rust Book G&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Rust_Book_G-154&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Rust_Book_G-154" id="mwDIY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIg">[</span>148<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDIo">Every two or three years, a new "edition" is produced. Editions are released to allow making limited <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breaking_changes" title="Breaking changes" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDIs">breaking changes</a>, such as promoting <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt895" id="mwDIw" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;await&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Rust&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;await&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><span class="k" id="mwDI0">await</span></code> to a keyword to support <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Async/await" title="Async/await" id="mwDI4">async/await</a> features. Crates targeting different editions can interoperate with each other, so a crate can upgrade to a new edition even if its callers or its dependencies still target older editions. Migration to a new edition can be assisted with automated tooling.<sup about="#mwt897" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall2021176–177_155-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall2021176–177&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall2021176–177-155&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Blandy&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Orendorff&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Tindall&quot;},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;pp&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;176–177&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBlandyOrendorffTindall2021176–177-155" id="mwDI8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJE">[</span>149<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="42" id="mwDJM" aria-labelledby="IDE_support"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="IDE_support">IDE support</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=42" title="Edit section: IDE support"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDJQ"><i id="mwDJU">rust-analyzer</i> is a set of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utility_software" title="Utility software" id="mwDJY">utilities</a> that provides <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_development_environment" title="Integrated development environment" id="mwDJc">integrated development environments</a> (IDEs) and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text_editor" title="Text editor" id="mwDJg">text editors</a> with information about a Rust project through the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Language_Server_Protocol" title="Language Server Protocol" id="mwDJk">Language Server Protocol</a>. This enables features including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autocomplete" title="Autocomplete" id="mwDJo">autocomplete</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compilation_error" title="Compilation error" id="mwDJs">compilation error</a> display, while editing code.<sup about="#mwt900" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023623_156-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023623&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023623-156&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2023&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;623&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols2023623-156" id="mwDJw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJ4">[</span>150<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJ8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="43" id="mwDKA" aria-labelledby="Performance"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Performance">Performance</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=43" title="Edit section: Performance"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDKE">Since it performs no garbage collection, Rust is often faster than other memory-safe languages.<sup about="#mwt908" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-157" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-157&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-157" id="mwDKI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKQ">[</span>151<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt909" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BeyondSafety_80-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;BeyondSafety&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-BeyondSafety-80" id="mwDKY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKg">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt912" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-158" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-158&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-158" id="mwDKo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKw">[</span>152<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDK0">]</span></span></a></sup> Most of Rust's memory safety guarantees impose no runtime overhead,<sup about="#mwt903" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202111_159-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMcNamara202111&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202111-159&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;McNamara&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;11&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202111-159" id="mwDK4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDK8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLA">[</span>153<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLE">]</span></span></a></sup> with the notable exception of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Array_(data_structure)" title="Array (data structure)" id="mwDLI">array indexing</a> which is checked at runtime by default.<sup about="#mwt915" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SaferAtAnySpeed_160-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;SaferAtAnySpeed&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-SaferAtAnySpeed-160&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-SaferAtAnySpeed-160" id="mwDLM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLU">[</span>154<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLY">]</span></span></a></sup> The performance impact of array indexing bounds checks varies, but can be significant in some cases.<sup about="#mwt916" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SaferAtAnySpeed_160-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;SaferAtAnySpeed&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-SaferAtAnySpeed-160" id="mwDLc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLk">[</span>154<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDLs">Many of Rust's features are so-called <i id="mwDLw">zero-cost abstractions</i>, meaning they are optimized away at compile time and incur no runtime penalty.<sup about="#mwt917" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202119,_27_161-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMcNamara202119, 27&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202119,_27-161&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;McNamara&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;19, 27&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202119,_27-161" id="mwDL0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDL4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDL8">[</span>155<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMA">]</span></span></a></sup> The ownership and borrowing system permits <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zero-copy" title="Zero-copy" id="mwDME">zero-copy</a> implementations for some performance-sensitive tasks, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parsing" title="Parsing" id="mwDMI">parsing</a>.<sup about="#mwt925" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-162" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-162&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-162" id="mwDMM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDMQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMU">[</span>156<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMY">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Static_dispatch" title="Static dispatch" id="mwDMc">Static dispatch</a> is used by default to eliminate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Method_call" title="Method call" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDMg">method calls</a>, except for methods called on dynamic trait objects.<sup about="#mwt920" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202120_163-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEMcNamara202120&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202120-163&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;McNamara&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;20&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcNamara202120-163" id="mwDMk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDMo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMs">[</span>157<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMw">]</span></span></a></sup> The compiler uses <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inline_expansion" title="Inline expansion" id="mwDM0">inline expansion</a> to eliminate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Function_call" title="Function call" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDM4">function calls</a> and statically dispatched method invocations.<sup about="#mwt928" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-164" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-164&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-164" id="mwDM8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNE">[</span>158<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDNM">Unlike C and C++, Rust allows the compiler to reorder struct and enum elements unless a <code id="mwDNQ">#[repr(C)]</code> representation attribute is applied.<sup about="#mwt934" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-165" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-165&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-165" id="mwDNU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNc">[</span>159<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNg">]</span></span></a></sup> This allows the compiler to produce more efficient code in some cases.<sup about="#mwt929" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGjengset202122_166-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEGjengset202122&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset202122-166&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Gjengset&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2021&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;22&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGjengset202122-166" id="mwDNk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNs">[</span>160<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDN0">Performance improvements in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LLVM" title="LLVM" id="mwDN4">LLVM</a> carry over to Rust.<sup about="#mwt937" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-how-fast-is-rust_167-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;how-fast-is-rust&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-how-fast-is-rust-167&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-how-fast-is-rust-167" id="mwDN8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDOA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOE">[</span>161<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="44" id="mwDOM" aria-labelledby="Adoption"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Adoption">Adoption</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=44" title="Edit section: Adoption"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt938" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDOQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;See also&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:See_also&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Category:Software programmed in Rust&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353705441" about="#mwt939" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Hatnote/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt938" id="mwDOU">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Software_programmed_in_Rust" title="Category:Software programmed in Rust">Category:Software programmed in Rust</a></div>
<!--
IMPORTANT:
Please add entries only with independent published sources, e.g., news articles, not GitHub projects with no secondary source(s). For specific guidelines, see: Wikipedia:Identifying reliable sources
-->
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDOY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Firefox_logo,_2019.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDOc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Firefox_logo,_2019.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Firefox_logo%2C_2019.svg/250px-Firefox_logo%2C_2019.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="512" data-file-type="drawing" height="150" width="150" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Firefox_logo%2C_2019.svg/330px-Firefox_logo%2C_2019.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDOg"></a><figcaption id="mwDOk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox" title="Firefox" id="mwDOo">Firefox</a> has components written in Rust as part of the underlying <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(software)" title="Gecko (software)" id="mwDOs">Gecko</a> browser engine</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDOw">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_service" title="Web service" id="mwDO0">web services</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenDNS" title="OpenDNS" id="mwDO4">OpenDNS</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DNS" title="DNS" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDO8">DNS</a> resolution service owned by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cisco" title="Cisco" id="mwDPA">Cisco</a>, uses Rust internally.<sup about="#mwt942" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-168" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-168&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-168" id="mwDPE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPM">[</span>162<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt945" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-169" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-169&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-169" id="mwDPU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPc">[</span>163<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPg">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Web_Services" title="Amazon Web Services" id="mwDPk">Amazon Web Services</a> uses Rust in "performance-sensitive components" of services. In 2019, AWS <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open_sourced" title="Open sourced" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDPo">open-sourced</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firecracker_(software)" title="Firecracker (software)" id="mwDPs">Firecracker</a>, a virtualization solution primarily written in Rust.<sup about="#mwt948" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-170" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-170&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-170" id="mwDPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDP4">[</span>164<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDP8">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Azure" title="Microsoft Azure" id="mwDQA">Microsoft Azure</a> IoT Edge, a platform used to run Azure services on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IoT" title="IoT" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDQE">IoT</a> devices, has components implemented in Rust.<sup about="#mwt951" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-171" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-171&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-171" id="mwDQI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQQ">[</span>165<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQU">]</span></span></a></sup> Microsoft also uses Rust to run containerized modules with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebAssembly" title="WebAssembly" id="mwDQY">WebAssembly</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kubernetes" title="Kubernetes" id="mwDQc">Kubernetes</a>.<sup about="#mwt954" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-172" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-172&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-172" id="mwDQg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQo">[</span>166<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQs">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloudflare" title="Cloudflare" id="mwDQw">Cloudflare</a>, a company providing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_delivery_network" title="Content delivery network" id="mwDQ0">content delivery network</a> services, used Rust to build a new <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_proxy" title="Web proxy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDQ4">web proxy</a> named Pingora for increased performance and efficiency.<sup about="#mwt957" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-173" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-173&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-173" id="mwDQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRE">[</span>167<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRI">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Npm" title="Npm" id="mwDRM">npm package manager</a> used Rust for its production authentication service in 2019.<sup about="#mwt960" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-174" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-174&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-174" id="mwDRQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRY">[</span>168<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt963" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-175" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-175&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-175" id="mwDRg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRo">[</span>169<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt966" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-176" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-176&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-176" id="mwDRw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDR0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDR4">[</span>170<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDR8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDSA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rust_for_Linux_logo.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDSE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rust_for_Linux_logo.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Rust_for_Linux_logo.svg/250px-Rust_for_Linux_logo.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="106" data-file-height="106" data-file-type="drawing" height="150" width="150" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Rust_for_Linux_logo.svg/330px-Rust_for_Linux_logo.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDSI"></a><figcaption id="mwDSM">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rust_for_Linux" title="Rust for Linux" id="mwDSQ">Rust for Linux</a> project has been supported in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_kernel" title="Linux kernel" id="mwDSU">Linux kernel</a> since 2022</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwDSY">In operating systems, the Linux kernel began introducing experimental support for Rust code in Version 6.1 in late 2022, as part of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rust_for_Linux" title="Rust for Linux" id="mwDSc">Rust for Linux</a> project.<sup about="#mwt969" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-UsenixRustForLinux_177-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;UsenixRustForLinux&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-UsenixRustForLinux-177&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-UsenixRustForLinux-177" id="mwDSg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDSk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSo">[</span>171<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt972" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-178" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-178&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-178" id="mwDSw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDS0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDS4">[</span>172<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDS8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt975" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-179" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-179&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-179" id="mwDTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTI">[</span>173<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTM">]</span></span></a></sup> The first drivers written in Rust were included in version 6.8.<sup about="#mwt976" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-UsenixRustForLinux_177-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;UsenixRustForLinux&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-UsenixRustForLinux-177" id="mwDTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTY">[</span>171<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTc">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025, kernel developers at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_Kernel_Developers_Summit" title="Linux Kernel Developers Summit" id="mwDTg">Linux Kernel Developers Summit</a> determined the project to be a success, and Rust usage for kernel code will no longer be considered experimental.<sup about="#mwt979" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-180" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-180&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-180" id="mwDTk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTs">[</span>174<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTw">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Android_(operating_system)" title="Android (operating system)" id="mwDT0">Android</a> developers used Rust in 2021 to rewrite existing components.<sup about="#mwt982" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-181" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-181&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-181" id="mwDT4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDT8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUA">[</span>175<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt985" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-182" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-182&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-182" id="mwDUI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUQ">[</span>176<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUU">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft" title="Microsoft" id="mwDUY">Microsoft</a> has rewritten parts of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows" title="Windows" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDUc">Windows</a> in Rust.<sup about="#mwt988" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-183" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-183&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-183" id="mwDUg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUo">[</span>177<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUs">]</span></span></a></sup> The r9 project aims to re-implement <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plan_9_from_Bell_Labs" title="Plan 9 from Bell Labs" id="mwDUw">Plan 9 from Bell Labs</a> in Rust.<sup about="#mwt991" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-184" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-184&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-184" id="mwDU0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDU4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDU8">[</span>178<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVA">]</span></span></a></sup> Rust has also been used in the development of new operating systems such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redox_(operating_system)" title="Redox (operating system)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDVE">Redox</a>, a "Unix-like" operating system and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microkernel" title="Microkernel" id="mwDVI">microkernel</a>,<sup about="#mwt994" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-185" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-185&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-185" id="mwDVM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVU">[</span>179<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVY">]</span></span></a></sup> Theseus, an experimental operating system with modular state management,<sup about="#mwt997" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-186" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-186&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-186" id="mwDVc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVk">[</span>180<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1000" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-187" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-187&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-187" id="mwDVs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDV0">[</span>181<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDV4">]</span></span></a></sup> and most of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuchsia_(operating_system)" title="Fuchsia (operating system)" id="mwDV8">Fuchsia</a>.<sup about="#mwt1003" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rustmag-1_188-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;rustmag-1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-rustmag-1-188&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-rustmag-1-188" id="mwDWA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWI">[</span>182<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWM">]</span></span></a></sup> Rust is used for command-line tools and operating system components such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stratis_(configuration_daemon)" title="Stratis (configuration daemon)" id="mwDWQ">stratisd</a>, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_system" title="File system" id="mwDWU">file system</a> manager<sup about="#mwt1006" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-189" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-189&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-189" id="mwDWY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWg">[</span>183<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1009" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-190" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-190&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-190" id="mwDWo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWw">[</span>184<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDW0">]</span></span></a></sup> and COSMIC, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desktop_environment" title="Desktop environment" id="mwDW4">desktop environment</a> by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System76" title="System76" id="mwDW8">System76</a>.<sup about="#mwt1012" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-191" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-191&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-191" id="mwDXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXI">[</span>185<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDXQ">In web development, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deno_(software)" title="Deno (software)" id="mwDXU">Deno</a>, a secure runtime for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JavaScript" title="JavaScript" id="mwDXY">JavaScript</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TypeScript" title="TypeScript" id="mwDXc">TypeScript</a>, is built on top of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V8_(JavaScript_engine)" title="V8 (JavaScript engine)" id="mwDXg">V8</a> using Rust and Tokio.<sup about="#mwt1015" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-192" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-192&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-192" id="mwDXk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXs">[</span>186<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXw">]</span></span></a></sup> Other notable adoptions in this space include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruffle_(software)" title="Ruffle (software)" id="mwDX0">Ruffle</a>, an open-source <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SWF" title="SWF" id="mwDX4">SWF</a> emulator,<sup about="#mwt1018" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-193" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-193&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-193" id="mwDX8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYE">[</span>187<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYI">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polkadot_(cryptocurrency)" title="Polkadot (cryptocurrency)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDYM">Polkadot</a>, an open source <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockchain" title="Blockchain" id="mwDYQ">blockchain</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cryptocurrency" title="Cryptocurrency" id="mwDYU">cryptocurrency</a> platform.<sup about="#mwt1021" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-194" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-194&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-194" id="mwDYY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDYc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYg">[</span>188<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYk">]</span></span></a></sup> Components from the Servo browser engine (funded by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla" title="Mozilla" id="mwDYo">Mozilla</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samsung" title="Samsung" id="mwDYs">Samsung</a>) were incorporated in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(software)" title="Gecko (software)" id="mwDYw">Gecko</a> browser engine underlying <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox" title="Firefox" id="mwDY0">Firefox</a>.<sup about="#mwt1024" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-195" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-195&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-195" id="mwDY4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDY8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZA">[</span>189<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZE">]</span></span></a></sup> In January 2023, Google (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alphabet_Inc." title="Alphabet Inc." id="mwDZI">Alphabet</a>) announced support for using third party Rust libraries in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chromium_(web_browser)" title="Chromium (web browser)" id="mwDZM">Chromium</a>.<sup about="#mwt1027" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-196" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-196&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-196" id="mwDZQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZY">[</span>190<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1030" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-197" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-197&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-197" id="mwDZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZo">[</span>191<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDZw">In other uses, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discord" title="Discord" id="mwDZ0">Discord</a>, an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant_messaging" title="Instant messaging" id="mwDZ4">instant messaging</a> software company, rewrote parts of its system in Rust for increased performance in 2020. In the same year, Dropbox announced that its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File_synchronization" title="File synchronization" id="mwDZ8">file synchronization</a> had been rewritten in Rust. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook" title="Facebook" id="mwDaA">Facebook</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms" title="Meta Platforms" id="mwDaE">Meta</a>) used Rust to redesign its system that manages source code for internal projects.<sup about="#mwt1031" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwDaI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDaM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaQ">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDaY">In the 2025 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stack_Overflow" title="Stack Overflow" id="mwDac">Stack Overflow</a> Developer Survey, 14.8% of respondents had recently done extensive development in Rust.<sup about="#mwt1040" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SO-2025-survey_198-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;SO-2025-survey&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-SO-2025-survey-198&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-SO-2025-survey-198" id="mwDag"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDak"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDao">[</span>192<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDas">]</span></span></a></sup> The survey named Rust the "most admired programming language" annually from 2016 to 2025 (inclusive), as measured by the number of existing developers interested in continuing to work in the language.<sup about="#mwt1043" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-199" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-199&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-199" id="mwDaw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDa0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDa4">[</span>193<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDa8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1032" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-200" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-200&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;refn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Refn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;note&quot;},&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;That is, among respondents who have done \&quot;extensive development work [with Rust] in over the past year\&quot; (14.8%), Rust had the largest percentage who also expressed interest to \&quot;work in [Rust] over the next year\&quot; (72.4%).<ref name=\&quot;SO-2025-survey\&quot;/>&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-200" data-mw-group="note" id="mwDbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbI">[</span>note 7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbM">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025, 29.2% of developers not currently working in Rust expressed an interest in doing so.<sup about="#mwt1044" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SO-2025-survey_198-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;SO-2025-survey&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-SO-2025-survey-198" id="mwDbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbY">[</span>192<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="45" id="mwDbg" aria-labelledby="In_academic_research"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="In_academic_research">In academic research</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=45" title="Edit section: In academic research"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDbk">Rust's safety and performance have been investigated in programming languages research.<sup about="#mwt1047" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-201" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-201&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-201" id="mwDbo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbw">[</span>194<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDb0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1048" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-UnsafeRustUse_119-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;UnsafeRustUse&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-UnsafeRustUse-119" id="mwDb4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDb8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcA">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1051" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-202" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-202&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-202" id="mwDcI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDcM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcQ">[</span>195<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDcY">In other fields, a journal article published to <i id="mwDcc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proceedings_of_the_International_Astronomical_Union" title="Proceedings of the International Astronomical Union" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDcg">Proceedings of the International Astronomical Union</a></i> used Rust to simulate multi-planet systems.<sup about="#mwt1054" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ResearchSoftware1_203-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ResearchSoftware1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-ResearchSoftware1-203&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-ResearchSoftware1-203" id="mwDck"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDco"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcs">[</span>196<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcw">]</span></span></a></sup> An article published in <i id="mwDc0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature_(journal)" title="Nature (journal)" id="mwDc4">Nature</a></i> shared stories of bioinformaticians using Rust.<sup about="#mwt1055" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Nature_147-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Nature&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Nature-147" id="mwDc8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdE">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdI">]</span></span></a></sup> Both articles cited Rust's performance and safety as advantages, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Learning_curve" title="Learning curve" id="mwDdM">learning curve</a> as being a primary drawback to Rust adoption.</p>

<p id="mwDdQ">The 2025 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DARPA" title="DARPA" id="mwDdU">DARPA</a> project TRACTOR aims to automatically translate C to Rust using techniques such as static analysis, dynamic analysis, and large language models.<sup about="#mwt1058" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-204" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-204&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-204" id="mwDdY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdg">[</span>197<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="46" id="mwDdo" aria-labelledby="Community"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Community">Community</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=46" title="Edit section: Community"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDds"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rustacean-orig-noshadow.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDdw"><img alt="A bright orange crab icon" resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rustacean-orig-noshadow.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Rustacean-orig-noshadow.svg/250px-Rustacean-orig-noshadow.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="341" data-file-type="drawing" height="167" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Rustacean-orig-noshadow.svg/500px-Rustacean-orig-noshadow.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDd0"></a><figcaption id="mwDd4">Some Rust users refer to themselves as Rustaceans (similar to the word <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crustacean" title="Crustacean" id="mwDd8">crustaceans</a>) and have adopted an orange crab, Ferris (shown above), as their unofficial mascot<sup about="#mwt1059" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20194_205-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20194&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20194-205&quot;},&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;sfn&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Sfn&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Klabnik&quot;},&quot;2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Nichols&quot;},&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;2019&quot;},&quot;p&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;4&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKlabnikNichols20194-205" id="mwDeA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDeE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeI">[</span>198<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1064" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-206" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-206&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-206" id="mwDeQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDeU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeY">[</span>199<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDec">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwDeg">According to the <i id="mwDek"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIT_Technology_Review" title="MIT Technology Review" id="mwDeo">MIT Technology Review</a></i>, the Rust community has been seen as "unusually friendly" to newcomers and particularly attracted people from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queer_community" title="Queer community" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDes">queer community</a>, partly due to its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Code_of_conduct" title="Code of conduct" id="mwDew">code of conduct</a>.<sup about="#mwt1065" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MITTechReview_24-18" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;MITTechReview&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-MITTechReview-24" id="mwDe0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDe4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDe8">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfA">]</span></span></a></sup> Inclusiveness has been cited as an important factor for some Rust developers.<sup about="#mwt1066" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Nature_147-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Nature&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Nature-147" id="mwDfE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfM">[</span>141<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The official Rust blog collects and publishes demographic data each year.<sup about="#mwt1069" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-StateOfRustSurvey2024_207-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;StateOfRustSurvey2024&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-StateOfRustSurvey2024-207&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-StateOfRustSurvey2024-207" id="mwDfU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfc">[</span>200<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="47" id="mwDfk" aria-labelledby="Rust_Foundation"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Rust_Foundation">Rust Foundation</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=47" title="Edit section: Rust Foundation"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1070" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDfo" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Infobox organization\n&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Infobox_organization&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rust Foundation&quot;},&quot;logo&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rust Foundation logo.png{{!}}class=skin-invert&quot;},&quot;formation&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{Start date and age|2021|02|08}}&quot;},&quot;founders&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{unbulleted list|[[Amazon Web Services]]|[[Google]]|[[Huawei]]|[[Microsoft]]|[[Mozilla Foundation]]}}&quot;},&quot;type&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[501(c)(6)]] organization<ref>{{Cite web |title=Anti-Bribery and Anti-Corruption Policy |url=https://rustfoundation.org/policy/anti-bribery-and-anti-corruption-policy/ |access-date=2026-06-03 |website=Rust Foundation |language=en-US}}</ref>&quot;},&quot;location&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[United States]]&quot;},&quot;leader_title&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[Chairperson]]&quot;},&quot;leader_name&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Shane Miller&quot;},&quot;leader_title2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;[[Executive Director]]&quot;},&quot;leader_name2&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Rebecca Rumbul&quot;},&quot;website&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;{{URL|foundation.rust-lang.org}}&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1358620234" about="#mwt1071" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Module:Infobox/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><table class="infobox vcard" about="#mwt1070" id="mwDfs"><caption class="infobox-title fn org">Rust Foundation</caption><tbody><tr><td colspan="2" class="infobox-image logo"><span class="mw-default-size skin-invert" typeof="mw:File/Frameless"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rust_Foundation_logo.png" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Rust_Foundation_logo.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Rust_Foundation_logo.png/250px-Rust_Foundation_logo.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="687" data-file-height="219" data-file-type="bitmap" height="80" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Rust_Foundation_logo.png/500px-Rust_Foundation_logo.png 2x" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1"></a></span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="padding-right:0.6em;">Formation</th><td class="infobox-data note">February<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>8, 2021<span class="noprint"><span typeof="mw:Entity">;</span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>5 years ago</span><span style="display:none"><span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>(<span class="bday dtstart published updated">2021-02-08</span>)</span></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="padding-right:0.6em;">Founders</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="mw-empty-elt"></span><div class="plainlist"><ul><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Web_Services" title="Amazon Web Services">Amazon Web Services</a></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google" title="Google">Google</a></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huawei" title="Huawei">Huawei</a></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft" title="Microsoft">Microsoft</a></li><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Foundation" title="Mozilla Foundation">Mozilla Foundation</a></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="padding-right:0.6em;">Type</th><td class="infobox-data"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/501(c)(6)" title="501(c)(6)" class="mw-redirect">501(c)(6)</a> organization<sup about="#mwt1075" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-208" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-208&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-208" id="mwDfw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDf0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDf4">[</span>201<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDf8">]</span></span></a></sup></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="padding-right:0.6em;">Location</th><td class="infobox-data label"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1126788409" about="#mwt1078" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;templatestyles&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;Plainlist/styles.css&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"></span><div class="plainlist"><ul><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States">United States</a></li></ul></div></td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="padding-right:0.6em;"><div style="display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0; "><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chairperson" title="Chairperson" class="mw-redirect">Chairperson</a></div></th><td class="infobox-data">Shane Miller</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="padding-right:0.6em;"><div style="display: inline-block; line-height: 1.2em; padding: .1em 0; "><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executive_Director" title="Executive Director" class="mw-redirect">Executive Director</a></div></th><td class="infobox-data">Rebecca Rumbul</td></tr><tr><th scope="row" class="infobox-label" style="padding-right:0.6em;">Website</th><td class="infobox-data"><span class="url"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://foundation.rust-lang.org" class="external text">foundation<wbr>.rust-lang<wbr>.org</a></span></td></tr></tbody></table>

<p id="mwDgA">The <b id="mwDgE">Rust Foundation</b> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-profit" title="Non-profit" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDgI">non-profit</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Membership_organization" title="Membership organization" id="mwDgM">membership organization</a> incorporated in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" id="mwDgQ">United States</a>; it manages the Rust trademark, infrastructure, and assets.<sup about="#mwt1081" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-209" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-209&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-209" id="mwDgU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgc">[</span>202<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1084" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_51-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;:4&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-:4-51&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-:4-51" id="mwDgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgs">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDg0">It was established on February 8, 2021, with five founding corporate members (Amazon Web Services, Huawei, Google, Microsoft, and Mozilla).<sup about="#mwt1087" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-210" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-210&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-210" id="mwDg4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDg8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhA">[</span>203<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhE">]</span></span></a></sup> The foundation's board was chaired by Shane Miller,<sup about="#mwt1090" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-211" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-211&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-211" id="mwDhI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhQ">[</span>204<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhU">]</span></span></a></sup> with Ashley Williams as interim executive director.<sup about="#mwt1091" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_51-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;:4&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-:4-51" id="mwDhY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhg">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhk">]</span></span></a></sup> In late 2021, Rebecca Rumbul became executive director and CEO.<!--Q109621019--><sup about="#mwt1094" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-212" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-212&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-212" id="mwDho"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhw">[</span>205<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDh0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="48" id="mwDh4" aria-labelledby="Governance_teams"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Governance_teams">Governance teams</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=48" title="Edit section: Governance teams"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDh8">The Rust project is maintained by 8 top-level <i id="mwDiA">teams</i> <span about="#mwt1095" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDiE" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;as of&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:As_of&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;November 2025&quot;},&quot;lc&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;y&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}">as of November 2025</span><sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;" about="#mwt1095"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup><span typeof="mw:Nowiki" about="#mwt1095"></span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements_from_November_2025" about="#mwt1095"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_containing_potentially_dated_statements" about="#mwt1095" id="mwDiI">: the leadership council, compiler team, dev tools team, infrastructure team, language team, launching pad, library team, and moderation team.<sup about="#mwt1098" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-213" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-213&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-213" id="mwDiM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDiQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiU">[</span>206<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiY">]</span></span></a></sup> The leadership council oversees the project and is formed by representatives among the other teams.<sup about="#mwt1101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-214" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-214&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-214" id="mwDic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDik">[</span>207<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDio">]</span></span></a></sup></p><!--<ref&#x3E;{{Cite web |first=Tim |last=Anderson |date=2021&#x2D;11&#x2D;23 |title=Entire Rust moderation team resigns |url=https://www.theregister.com/2021/11/23/rust_moderation_team_quits/ |access&#x2D;date=2024&#x2D;01&#x2D;12 |website=The Register |language=en}}</ref&#x3E;-->

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="49" id="mwDis" aria-labelledby="See_also"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="See_also">See also</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=49" title="Edit section: See also"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<ul id="mwDiw"><li id="mwDi0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_programming_languages" title="List of programming languages" id="mwDi4">List of programming languages</a></li>
<li id="mwDi8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Rust_software_and_tools" title="List of Rust software and tools" id="mwDjA">List of Rust software and tools</a></li>
<li id="mwDjE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_the_Rust_programming_language" title="Outline of the Rust programming language" id="mwDjI">Outline of the Rust programming language</a></li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="50" id="mwDjM" aria-labelledby="Notes"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Notes">Notes</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=50" title="Edit section: Notes"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1102" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDjQ" data-mw="{&quot;parts&quot;:[{&quot;template&quot;:{&quot;target&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;Reflist&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:&quot;./Template:Reflist&quot;},&quot;params&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:{&quot;wt&quot;:&quot;note&quot;}},&quot;i&quot;:0}}]}"></span><div about="#mwt1102" id="mwDjU">
<div class="mw-references-wrap" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt1104" id="mwDjY" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;references&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;group&quot;:&quot;note&quot;,&quot;responsive&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;&quot;}}"><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="note" id="mwDjc"><li about="#cite_note-3" id="cite_note-3" data-mw-footnote-number="1"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDjg"><a href="#cite_ref-3" data-mw-group="note" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDjk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDjo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-3" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="note">Including build tools, host tools, and standard library support for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X86-64" title="X86-64" id="mwDjs">x86-64</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ARM_architecture_family" title="ARM architecture family" id="mwDjw">ARM</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIPS_architecture" title="MIPS architecture" id="mwDj0">MIPS</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RISC-V" title="RISC-V" id="mwDj4">RISC-V</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebAssembly" title="WebAssembly" id="mwDj8">WebAssembly</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I686" title="I686" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDkA">i686</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AArch64" title="AArch64" id="mwDkE">AArch64</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PowerPC" title="PowerPC" id="mwDkI">PowerPC</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_on_IBM_Z" title="Linux on IBM Z" id="mwDkM">s390x</a>.<sup about="#mwt17" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CrossPlatform_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;CrossPlatform&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-CrossPlatform-2&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-CrossPlatform-2" id="mwDkQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDkU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkY">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkc">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-4" id="cite_note-4" data-mw-footnote-number="2"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDkg"><a href="#cite_ref-4" data-mw-group="note" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDkk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDko">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-4" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="note">Including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows" title="Windows" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDks">Windows</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux" title="Linux" id="mwDkw">Linux</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacOS" title="MacOS" id="mwDk0">macOS</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FreeBSD" title="FreeBSD" id="mwDk4">FreeBSD</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NetBSD" title="NetBSD" id="mwDk8">NetBSD</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illumos" title="Illumos" id="mwDlA">Illumos</a>. Host build tools on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Android_(operating_system)" title="Android (operating system)" id="mwDlE">Android</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOS" title="IOS" id="mwDlI">iOS</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haiku_(operating_system)" title="Haiku (operating system)" id="mwDlM">Haiku</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redox_(operating_system)" title="Redox (operating system)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDlQ">Redox</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuchsia_(operating_system)" title="Fuchsia (operating system)" id="mwDlU">Fuchsia</a> are not officially shipped; these operating systems are supported as targets.<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CrossPlatform_2-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;CrossPlatform&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-CrossPlatform-2" id="mwDlY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlk">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-7" id="cite_note-7" data-mw-footnote-number="3"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDlo"><a href="#cite_ref-7" data-mw-group="note" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDls"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDlw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-7" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="note">Third-party dependencies, e.g., <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LLVM" title="LLVM" id="mwDl0">LLVM</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MSVC" title="MSVC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDl4">MSVC</a>, are subject to their own licenses.<sup about="#mwt31" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-5&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwDl8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmE">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt34" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-licenses_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;licenses&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-licenses-6" id="mwDmM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmU">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmY">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-nil-10" id="cite_note-nil-10" data-mw-footnote-number="4"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDmc"><a href="#cite_ref-nil_10-0" data-mw-group="note" id="mwDmg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDmk">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-nil_10-1" data-mw-group="note" id="mwDmo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDms">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-nil-10" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="note">NIL is cited as an influence for Rust in multiple sources; this likely refers to Network Implementation Language developed by Robert Strom and others at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM" title="IBM" id="mwDmw">IBM</a>, which pioneered <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typestate_analysis" title="Typestate analysis" id="mwDm0">typestate analysis</a>,<sup about="#mwt44" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Strom1983_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Strom1983&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Strom1983-8&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Strom1983-8" id="mwDm4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDm8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt49" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-9&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-9" id="mwDnI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDnM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnU">]</span></span></a></sup> not to be confused with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NIL_(programming_language)" title="NIL (programming language)" id="mwDnY">New Implementation of LISP</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-30" id="cite_note-30" data-mw-footnote-number="5"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDnc"><a href="#cite_ref-30" data-mw-group="note" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDng"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDnk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-30" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="note">The list of Rust compiler versions (referred to as a bootstrapping chain) has history going back to 2012.<sup about="#mwt147" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Nelson2022RustConf_29-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Nelson2022RustConf&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-Nelson2022RustConf-29&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-Nelson2022RustConf-29" id="mwDno"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDns"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnw">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDn0">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-133" id="cite_note-133" data-mw-footnote-number="6"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDn4"><a href="#cite_ref-133" data-mw-group="note" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDn8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDoA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-133" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="note">wrapping <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-text mw-content-ltr" style="" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt787" id="mwDoE" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;text&quot;,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;style&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;no_mangle&quot;}}">no_mangle</code> with <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt788" id="mwDoI" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;}}"><span class="k" id="mwDoM">unsafe</span></code> as well as prefacing the <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt789" id="mwDoQ" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;extern \&quot;C\&quot;&quot;}}"><span class="k" id="mwDoU">extern</span><span class="w" id="mwDoY"> </span><span class="s" id="mwDoc">"C"</span></code> block with <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-rust mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr" typeof="mw:Extension/syntaxhighlight" about="#mwt790" id="mwDog" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;syntaxhighlight&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;lang&quot;:&quot;rust&quot;,&quot;inline&quot;:&quot;1&quot;},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;extsrc&quot;:&quot;unsafe&quot;}}"><span class="k" id="mwDok">unsafe</span></code> are required in the 2024 edition or later.<sup about="#mwt793" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-132" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{},&quot;body&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;mw-reference-text-cite_note-132&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-132" id="mwDoo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDos"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDow">[</span>127<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDo0">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-200" id="cite_note-200" data-mw-footnote-number="7"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDo4"><a href="#cite_ref-200" data-mw-group="note" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDo8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDpA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-200" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="note">That is, among respondents who have done "extensive development work [with Rust] in over the past year" (14.8%), Rust had the largest percentage who also expressed interest to "work in [Rust] over the next year" (72.4%).<sup about="#mwt1033" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SO-2025-survey_198-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw="{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;ref&quot;,&quot;attrs&quot;:{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;SO-2025-survey&quot;}}"><a href="#cite_note-SO-2025-survey-198" id="mwDpE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpM">[</span>192<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpQ">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
</ol></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="51" id="mwDpU" aria-labelledby="References"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="References">References</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Rust_(programming_language)&amp;action=edit&amp;section=51" title="Edit section: References"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
